{"raw": {"https://stfrancis.peopleadmin.com/postings/5907": {"title": "Retention Specialist", "description": "University of St. Francis Employment Opportunities | Retention Specialist Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help USF Website About Us Saints Stats Mission & History USF is Nationally Ranked Leadership Take a Virtual Tour USF Alumni & Family Relations Notice of Nondiscrimination Retention Specialist Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to\u00a0bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. \u00a0If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Job Title Retention Specialist Position Number XXXXXX-XX Department Office of the Provost Job Grade 7 Anticipated Salary Range $18.86 - $20.73 Benefits Not benefit eligible Notice of Nondiscrimination The University of St. Francis does not discriminate in its employment practices or in its educational programs on the basis of any protected class. The University also prohibits retaliation against any person opposing discrimination or harassment or participating in any internal or external investigation or complaint process related to allegations of misconduct. For a complete copy of USF\u2019s Policy on Equal Opportunity, Harassment, and Nondiscrimination for All Faculty, Students, Employees and Third Parties or for more information, please go to https://www.stfrancis.edu/titleix/ or contact the Title IX Coordinator at TitleIX@stfrancis.edu. Position Summary The Retention Specialist reports to the Provost and will support student retention across the university, especially in the areas of academic success, transition to college, and co-curricular/athletic responsibilities. This is a part-time, temporary position that will be evaluated at the conclusion of the 2026-2027 academic year, and may or may not be extended at that time. Essential Duties & Responsibilities ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Collaborate with Athletics, Student Affairs, academic departments, and other campus partners to coordinate student support, share relevant concerns, and connect students with appropriate services Provide proactive support and early intervention for students by helping them navigate academic expectations, connect with campus resources, and resolve barriers that may affect persistence Support retention and completion goals for the university by coordinating timely outreach and contributing to retention-focused data review and follow-up Monitor and respond to early alert referrals by communicating with faculty, staff, and coaches; conduct outreach to students, and document follow-up actions Provide general student support Create a welcoming community and engage in university mission Participate in and promote a culture of continuing quality improvement Other related duties as assigned Minimum Requirements Bachelor\u2019s degree Commitment to serving students with a focus on positive relationships Strong organizational skills and attention to detail Good communication and interpersonal skills with an understanding of FERPA Willingness to collaborate across units Ability to work effectively within a team and take initiative individually Willingness to support the Catholic and Franciscan values of the university Preferred Requirements Master\u2019s degree Two years of professional experience in higher education Experience with student athletes Hours/Shift/Work Schedule Part-time position working 20 hours per week. This is a part-time, temporary position that will be evaluated at the conclusion of the 2026-2027 academic year, and may or may not be extended at that time. Physical Requirements of Position Work is performed in an office setting with minimal exposure to health or safety hazards. Substantial time is spent working on a computer. This is sedentary work which requires the following physical activities: sitting, walking, bending, stooping, finger dexterity, repetitive motions, talking, hearing and visual acuity. Posting Detail Information Posting Number FP0811-16 Open Date 10/13/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you willing to uphold the Catholic and Franciscan values of the University? Yes No * Do you have, or exceed, the minimum amount of relevant work experience as listed in our posting? Yes No * Will you now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status (e.g., H-1B visa status)? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Transcripts (unofficial are acceptable at time of application) Mission Response at https://pa-hrsuite-production.s3.amazonaws.com/856/docs/67939.pdf Optional Documents Reference List - names and contact information of 3 additional references The Annual Security & Fire Safety Report is published in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act. Clery - 2021 University of St. Francis Annual Security and Fire Safety Report A paper copy of this report is available by contacting the Safety & Security office at 815-740-3200. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://stfrancis.peopleadmin.com/postings/5906": {"title": "Residence Life Coordinator", "description": "University of St. Francis Employment Opportunities | Residence Life Coordinator Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help USF Website About Us Saints Stats Mission & History USF is Nationally Ranked Leadership Take a Virtual Tour USF Alumni & Family Relations Notice of Nondiscrimination Residence Life Coordinator Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to\u00a0bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. \u00a0If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Job Title Residence Life Coordinator Position Number 006602 Department Residence Education - Joliet IL main campus Job Grade 7 Anticipated Salary Range $43,888 Benefits https://stfrancis.edu/employment Notice of Nondiscrimination The University of St. Francis does not discriminate in its employment practices or in its educational programs on the basis of any protected class. The University also prohibits retaliation against any person opposing discrimination or harassment or participating in any internal or external investigation or complaint process related to allegations of misconduct. For a complete copy of USF\u2019s Policy on Equal Opportunity, Harassment, and Nondiscrimination for All Faculty, Students, Employees and Third Parties or for more information, please go to https://www.stfrancis.edu/titleix/ or contact the Title IX Coordinator at TitleIX@stfrancis.edu. Position Summary Under the direction of the Dean of Student Life, the Residence Life Coordinator serves as the primary professional staff member responsible for on-campus housing and oversees all aspects of the residential experience (community development, housing operations, student staff supervision, conduct, crisis response) for the University\u2019s residence halls. This live-in position calls for a versatile, mission-driven practitioner who can move fluidly between leadership of the student residential staff and daily operations management, cultivating community for up to approximately 300-400 residential students rooted in our values-based approach to the Catholic Franciscan tradition. Essential Duties & Responsibilities \u00b7\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0Provide daily operations management of the University\u2019s residence life and housing program, ensuring alignment with institutional mission, policies, and strategic priorities. \u00b7\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0Oversee housing operations, including applications, assignments, occupancy, room changes, openings/closings, inspections, and break housing. \u00b7\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0Manage the residence life budget, records, housing software, and reporting in consultation with the Dean of Student Life. \u00b7\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0Coordinate with Facilities, Safety and Security, Dining Services, Admissions, and other departments on residential operations, including summer conferences and camps. \u00b7\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0Foster safe, welcoming, and engaged residential communities that promote student learning, belonging, personal development, and retention. \u00b7\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0Maintain a visible and accessible presence, building meaningful relationships with residential students. \u00b7\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0Develop residential programming and community standards that reflect the University\u2019s Catholic and Franciscan mission while welcoming students of all faith backgrounds. \u00b7\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0Address routine residential conduct matters through educational and restorative approaches; refer serious cases to the Dean of Student Life and recommend policy improvements as appropriate. \u00b7\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0Participate in the weekly professional staff crisis response rotation, coordinating with Campus Safety & Security, Crisis Management, and student staff. \u00b7\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0Respond to emergencies with appropriate judgment, documentation, and follow-up. \u00b7\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0Identify and refer students of concern to appropriate campus resources; participate in the University\u2019s CARE team and collaborate with Athletics as needed. \u00b7\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0Participate in University committees and support major campus events, including Pre-Orientation, Orientation/Welcome Weekend, Homecoming, and Commencements. \u00b7\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0Collaborate across Mission & Student Affairs to advance student success, retention, and mission integration. \u00b7\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0Perform other duties as assigned. Minimum Requirements Bachelor\u2019s degree with relevant experience. Two to four years of progressive experience in residence life or housing, with demonstrated capacity for independent leadership of a program or functional area. Demonstrated skills in supervision, housing operations, conflict resolution, and crisis response. Strong organizational, administrative, budgetary, and communication skills; ability to work autonomously and manage competing priorities. Willingness to enthusiastically support the Catholic Franciscan mission of the University and to foster an environment welcoming to students of all backgrounds. Preferred Requirements Master\u2019s degree in Higher Education, Student Affairs, Counseling, or a related field. Experience serving as the lead or sole professional for a residential program or hall. Familiarity with residential curriculum models and assessment of student learning. Experience with housing management systems and occupancy reporting. Hours/Shift/Work Schedule Approximately 40 hours per week (Monday through Friday), primarily days, with evening, weekend, and holiday responsibilities (essential functions of the role). Live-in requirement: This is a required live-in position. A furnished on-campus apartment and campus parking are provided in addition to salary. On-call requirement: Participation in the crisis phone duty rotation is an essential function of the position. When serving on duty, the Coordinator must adhere to departmental policy which includes remain within a 15-minute drive of campus and be able to respond in person to emergencies. Evening, weekend, and holiday responsibilities are essential functions of the role. Physical Requirements of Position Work is performed in an office setting with minimal exposure to health or safety hazards. Substantial time is spent working on a computer. This is sedentary work which requires the following physical activities: sitting, walking, bending, stooping, finger dexterity, repetitive motions, talking, hearing and visual acuity. Posting Detail Information Posting Number FP0810-16 Open Date 10/09/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you willing to uphold the Catholic and Franciscan values of the University? Yes No * Will you now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status (e.g., H-1B visa status)? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Transcripts (unofficial are acceptable at time of application) Mission Response at https://pa-hrsuite-production.s3.amazonaws.com/856/docs/67939.pdf Optional Documents The Annual Security & Fire Safety Report is published in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act. Clery - 2021 University of St. Francis Annual Security and Fire Safety Report A paper copy of this report is available by contacting the Safety & Security office at 815-740-3200. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://stfrancis.peopleadmin.com/postings/5905": {"title": "Security Officer - full time", "description": "University of St. Francis Employment Opportunities | Security Officer - full time Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help USF Website About Us Saints Stats Mission & History USF is Nationally Ranked Leadership Take a Virtual Tour USF Alumni & Family Relations Notice of Nondiscrimination Security Officer - full time Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to\u00a0bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. \u00a0If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Job Title Security Officer - full time Position Number 006230-00 Department Safety & Security - Joliet, IL Job Grade 5 Anticipated Salary Range $15.02 - $16.52 Benefits https://stfrancis.edu/employment/ Notice of Nondiscrimination The University of St. Francis does not discriminate in its employment practices or in its educational programs on the basis of any protected class. The University also prohibits retaliation against any person opposing discrimination or harassment or participating in any internal or external investigation or complaint process related to allegations of misconduct. For a complete copy of USF\u2019s Policy on Equal Opportunity, Harassment, and Nondiscrimination for All Faculty, Students, Employees and Third Parties or for more information, please go to https://www.stfrancis.edu/titleix/ or contact the Title IX Coordinator at TitleIX@stfrancis.edu. Position Summary To provide safety and security services for the protection of life and property to the university community. Essential Duties & Responsibilities Patrol assigned areas (university buildings, dormitories, parking lots) on foot or in a vehicle to ensure security, and to make presence known in a manner that contributes to the deterrence of security breaches Provide escort services for visitors, students, staff, faculty, and individuals responsible for transportation of monies to or from university Prepare written and computerized reports of daily activity and incidents occurring in, on or around campus property Provide visible patrol and observe and report irregularities, such as fire hazards, leaking water pipes, missing signs, deficient parking lot surface conditions, and security doors left unlocked; sound alarm in case of fire or presence of unauthorized persons Perform periodic checks of emergency call boxes and/or streetlights to ensure proper functioning; report malfunctions Provide visible patrol and examine doors, windows, and gates to determine if they are secure Drive university vehicles, providing for the safe and efficient transportation to the university community and visitors Provide public assistance when requested, including lockout services and information Remains alert for the presence of unauthorized persons or violators, address security breaches and suspicious persons and notifies police authorities as needed Participate and pass annual/semi-annual training classes including but not limited to NIMS (National Incident Management System), First Aid/Narcan\u00ae, ASP (Armament Systems and Procedures) baton and handcuffing and any computer-based online training Perform other duties or assignments as required Participate in and promote a culture of continuing quality improvement Minimum Requirements 21 years of age High school diploma or GED Possess a valid Illinois driver\u2019s license Provision of a clear background check Ability to perform physical requirements of the position Ability to read, analyze and interpret instructions Ability to understand and adhere to all Safety and Security rules, regulations, policy and procedures, written memorandums, and verbal instructions issued by the director or his designee Ability to communicate effectively both orally and in writing Ability to apply firm and courteous instructions with the students, employees and visitors Ability to analyze situations quickly and objectively take the appropriate course of action Ability to establish and maintain cordial and effective working relationships with the university community Ability to gather data, compile information and prepare reports. Availability to work a varied work schedule encompassing all shifts Willingness to support the Catholic and Franciscan values of the university Preferred Requirements Hours/Shift/Work Schedule This is a full-time, non-exempt position which consists of eight-hour varied shifts on multiple campuses including nights and weekends. Schedule will include some holidays. The Safety & Security Department operates 24/7. Physical Requirements of Position This position requires the ability to walk, sit or stand for extended periods of time, run when necessary, climb stairs, lift up to 50 lbs. with no assistance, and to work in adverse weather conditions. The noise level in the work environment may sometimes be loud. Some work will be performed on a computer in an office setting with minimal exposure to health or safety hazards. Also requires the ability to perform the following physical activities: sitting, walking, bending, stooping, finger dexterity, repetitive motions, talking, hearing and visual acuity. Posting Detail Information Posting Number FP0808-16 Open Date 10/06/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled No Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you willing to uphold the Catholic and Franciscan values of the University? Yes No * Please indicate your highest level of completed education: Less than GED/high school diploma GED/high school diploma Bachelor's degree Master's degree ABD Doctorate * How many years of experience do you have in this type of position? 0-1 1-3 3-5 5-7 7+ How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other * Are you at least 21 years old? Yes No * Please indicate your highest level of completed education: Less than GED/high school diploma GED/high school diploma Bachelor's degree Master's degree ABD Doctorate * Do you have a valid Illinois driver's license? Yes No * Please indicate your availability to work: I am available to work any shift as needed. I am available to work day shift only. I am available to work 2nd shift only. I am available to work 3rd shift only. * How many years of experience do you have in this type of position? 0-1 1-3 3-5 5-7 7+ * Will you now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status (e.g., H-1B visa status)? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Mission Response at https://pa-hrsuite-production.s3.amazonaws.com/856/docs/67939.pdf Optional Documents Cover Letter Letter of Recommendation 1 (you must upload something; letter writers may  send directly to Working@stfrancis.edu) The Annual Security & Fire Safety Report is published in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act. Clery - 2021 University of St. Francis Annual Security and Fire Safety Report A paper copy of this report is available by contacting the Safety & Security office at 815-740-3200. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://stfrancis.peopleadmin.com/postings/5902": {"title": "Graduate Assistant for Student Life", "description": "University of St. Francis Employment Opportunities | Graduate Assistant for Student Life Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help USF Website About Us Saints Stats Mission & History USF is Nationally Ranked Leadership Take a Virtual Tour USF Alumni & Family Relations Notice of Nondiscrimination Graduate Assistant for Student Life Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to\u00a0bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. \u00a0If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Job Title Graduate Assistant for Student Life Position Number GA6600 Department Residence Education - Joliet IL main campus Job Grade Anticipated Salary Range $5000 Stipend (in addition to Graduate Tuition Remission, Room/Board) Benefits Graduate Tuition Remission, Room/Board Notice of Nondiscrimination The University of St. Francis does not discriminate in its employment practices or in its educational programs on the basis of any protected class. The University also prohibits retaliation against any person opposing discrimination or harassment or participating in any internal or external investigation or complaint process related to allegations of misconduct. For a complete copy of USF\u2019s Policy on Equal Opportunity, Harassment, and Nondiscrimination for All Faculty, Students, Employees and Third Parties or for more information, please go to https://www.stfrancis.edu/titleix/ or contact the Title IX Coordinator at TitleIX@stfrancis.edu. Position Summary The Graduate Assistant for Student Life supports programs and services that strengthen student engagement, belonging, leadership, and campus community. The position works closely with Student Life staff and student leaders in the areas of campus programming, student clubs and organizations, the Student Activities Board ( SAB ), intramurals, Greek Life, and both commuter engagement and residential life. The Graduate Assistant resides on campus and participates in the residence hall on-call rotation. Essential Duties & Responsibilities \u00b7 Support the mission, vision, values, and Franciscan traditions of the University of St. Francis. \u00b7 Assist with the planning and implementation of Student Life programs, activities, and campus traditions which support student belonging and retention. \u00b7 Coordinate campus-wide student activities and intramurals with the support of the Student Activities Board ( SAB ) and Commuter Assistants for residential and commuter students, including program logistics, communications, contracts, purchasing, budget tracking, assessment, and other administrative responsibilities as directed. \u00b7 Support and advise student leaders in student clubs and organizations and Greek Life. \u00b7 Participate in the residence hall emergency response/on-call rotation and assist with residential student needs as assigned. \u00b7 Attend Student Life and Division staff meetings, and other meetings or events as appropriate. \u00b7 Collaborate with other offices to support a welcoming and engaging campus environment. \u00b7 Perform other duties and special projects as assigned by the supervisor. Minimum Requirements \u00b7 Bachelor\u2019s degree required. \u00b7 Must be admitted to and remain in good standing in an eligible University of St. Francis graduate program. \u00b7 Experience in student affairs, student leadership, campus programming, residence life, or related areas preferred. \u00b7 Strong interpersonal, organizational, communication, and administrative skills. \u00b7 Ability to work effectively with students, faculty, staff, and other campus constituencies. \u00b7 Willingness to work evenings and weekends and to participate in the residence hall on-call rotation. \u00b7 Commitment to the mission, vision, values, and traditions of the University of St. Francis. Preferred Requirements Hours/Shift/Work Schedule Approximately 20 hours a week, established in accordance with the University\u2019s Graduate Assistant Policy with evening and weekend responsibilities required, in addition to residence hall on-call duty. Physical Requirements of Position The Graduate Assistant resides on campus as part of the appointment. Work is performed primarily in campus office, program, and residential settings and requires regular interaction with students. Evening and weekend work is expected based on programs, events, and on-call responsibilities. During on-call responsibilities, the Graduate Assistant must adhere to applicable institutional policies including remaining within a 15-minute travel radius from the Main Campus at all times and able to respond to emergencies. Posting Detail Information Posting Number FP0809-16 Open Date 10/09/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you willing to uphold the Catholic and Franciscan values of the University? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Mission Response at https://pa-hrsuite-production.s3.amazonaws.com/856/docs/67939.pdf Optional Documents The Annual Security & Fire Safety Report is published in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act. Clery - 2021 University of St. Francis Annual Security and Fire Safety Report A paper copy of this report is available by contacting the Safety & Security office at 815-740-3200. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://stfrancis.peopleadmin.com/postings/5900": {"title": "Art &amp; Design Student Worker", "description": "University of St. Francis Employment Opportunities | Art &amp; Design Student Worker Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help USF Website About Us Saints Stats Mission & History USF is Nationally Ranked Leadership Take a Virtual Tour USF Alumni & Family Relations Notice of Nondiscrimination Art & Design Student Worker Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to\u00a0bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. \u00a0If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information First Section Job Title Art & Design Student Worker Position Number xxxxx-xx Organizational Unit Art & Design Student Workers - Rialto Theater, Joliet IL Posting Number SP0949-16 Notice of Nondiscrimination The University of St. Francis does not discriminate in its employment practices or in its educational programs on the basis of any protected class. The University also prohibits retaliation against any person opposing discrimination or harassment or participating in any internal or external investigation or complaint process related to allegations of misconduct. For a complete copy of USF\u2019s Policy on Equal Opportunity, Harassment, and Nondiscrimination for All Faculty, Students, Employees and Third Parties or for more information, please go to https://www.stfrancis.edu/titleix/ or contact the Title IX Coordinator at TitleIX@stfrancis.edu. Requirements Responsibilities Work with Art & Design faculty to update software in the Mac digital lab Assist students and faculty in studio art classes Work with faculty to maintain the Moser Performing Arts Center ( MPAC ) GalleryL Layout exhibitions Assist faculty with studio class preparation Assist with the installations of art shows at the MPAC \u2013 Moser Performing Arts Center Gallery. Qualifications Minimum Requirements Preferably an Art & Design major or minor. Knowledge of studio art practices. Understanding of digital media. Willingness to work with the person managing the art gallery in Tower Hall Preferred Requirements Junior or senior standing as an Art & Design major. Eligible for federal work-study. Pay Rate Hourly $15.00 Benefits Not-benefit eligibile Hours / Week 5-10 hours Close Date Quick Link https://stfrancis.peopleadmin.com/postings/5897 Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter Letter of Recommendation 1 (you must upload something; letter writers may  send directly to Working@stfrancis.edu) Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you willing to uphold the Catholic and Franciscan values of the University? Yes No * Are you eligible for the Federal Work Study Award in your Financial Aid package? Yes No The Annual Security & Fire Safety Report is published in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act. Clery - 2021 University of St. Francis Annual Security and Fire Safety Report A paper copy of this report is available by contacting the Safety & Security office at 815-740-3200. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://stfrancis.peopleadmin.com/postings/5887": {"title": "Financial Aid Services Student Worker", "description": "University of St. Francis Employment Opportunities | Financial Aid Services Student Worker Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help USF Website About Us Saints Stats Mission & History USF is Nationally Ranked Leadership Take a Virtual Tour USF Alumni & Family Relations Notice of Nondiscrimination Financial Aid Services Student Worker Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to\u00a0bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. \u00a0If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information First Section Job Title Financial Aid Services Student Worker Position Number ST3671 Organizational Unit Financial Aid Services Student Workers - Joliet IL Posting Number SP0947-16 Notice of Nondiscrimination The University of St. Francis does not discriminate in its employment practices or in its educational programs on the basis of any protected class. The University also prohibits retaliation against any person opposing discrimination or harassment or participating in any internal or external investigation or complaint process related to allegations of misconduct. For a complete copy of USF\u2019s Policy on Equal Opportunity, Harassment, and Nondiscrimination for All Faculty, Students, Employees and Third Parties or for more information, please go to https://www.stfrancis.edu/titleix/ or contact the Title IX Coordinator at TitleIX@stfrancis.edu. Requirements Responsibilities Assist and provide support to front desk staff and counselors as needed. Service new and current families by providing excellent customer service answering phones, processing incoming mail, and other duties as assigned. Answer student/family phone inquiries, and provide excellent customer service and information. (Communication, Critical Thinking, Professionalism) Respond to student/family email inquiries, and provide excellent customer service and information. (Communication, Critical Thinking, Professionalism) Process in-coming mail. (Professionalism, Communication) Assist with completing FAFSA applications. (Communication, Critical Thinking, Professionalism, Equity and Inclusion) Assist walk-in students with questions and provide excellent customer service and information. (Communication, Critical Thinking, Equity and Inclusion, Professionalism) Maintain filing system. (Professionalism) Work reports as required. (Communication, Critical Thinking, Professionalism, Team Work, Technology) Other duties as assigned Qualifications Current or Registered USF students in good academic standing Federal Work-Study ( FWS ) eligible Must have attention to detail and good organizational skills Spanish speaking (preferred) Pay Rate Hourly 15 Benefits Not Benefit Eligible Hours / Week 10 Close Date Quick Link https://stfrancis.peopleadmin.com/postings/5886 Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you willing to uphold the Catholic and Franciscan values of the University? Yes No The Annual Security & Fire Safety Report is published in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act. Clery - 2021 University of St. Francis Annual Security and Fire Safety Report A paper copy of this report is available by contacting the Safety & Security office at 815-740-3200. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://stfrancis.peopleadmin.com/postings/5884": {"title": "Marian Desk Worker", "description": "University of St. Francis Employment Opportunities | Marian Desk Worker Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help USF Website About Us Saints Stats Mission & History USF is Nationally Ranked Leadership Take a Virtual Tour USF Alumni & Family Relations Notice of Nondiscrimination Marian Desk Worker Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to\u00a0bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. \u00a0If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information First Section Job Title Marian Desk Worker Position Number ST6600-00 Organizational Unit Residence Hall Student Workers - Joliet IL Posting Number SP0946-16 Notice of Nondiscrimination The University of St. Francis does not discriminate in its employment practices or in its educational programs on the basis of any protected class. The University also prohibits retaliation against any person opposing discrimination or harassment or participating in any internal or external investigation or complaint process related to allegations of misconduct. For a complete copy of USF\u2019s Policy on Equal Opportunity, Harassment, and Nondiscrimination for All Faculty, Students, Employees and Third Parties or for more information, please go to https://www.stfrancis.edu/titleix/ or contact the Title IX Coordinator at TitleIX@stfrancis.edu. Requirements Responsibilities Answer phones; transfer calls and responding to other forms of electronic communication (Communication) Customer Service: assist with the greeting of visitor\u2019s and handling inquiries from the public (Professionalism) Assist with event promotion and advertisement of on campus activities (Critical Thinking) Assists with the management of opening, closing and vacation periods within the residence halls (Teamwork) Various customer service activities (Professionalism) Assist in maintaining a secure living environment through proper policy enforcement (Professionalism) Other duties as assigned by supervisor and/or Residence Education staff (Teamwork) Participate in and promote a culture of continuing quality improvement Qualifications MINIMUM : Current USF student in good standing Minimum GPA of 2.5 A commitment to quality customer service Positive attitude Strong leadership and interpersonal skills High level of maturity and responsibility Satisfactory computer skills within Word and Excel in Microsoft Office Willingness to support the Catholic and Franciscan values of the University Ability to lift at least 30 pounds, with or without accommodation Ability to pass background check PREFERRED : Comfortable working in a fast-paced environment with individuals of all ages (specifically young adults from ages 18-25 years old) Experience with e-mail programs such as Microsoft Outlook Strong administrative skills and attention to detail is a plus Pay Rate Hourly $15 Benefits Not benefit eligible Hours / Week 20 Close Date Quick Link https://stfrancis.peopleadmin.com/postings/5883 Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Letter of Recommendation 1 (you must upload something; letter writers may  send directly to Working@stfrancis.edu) Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently enrolled at USF as either a full-time undergrad or a part-time graduate student, and in good standing? Yes No * Are you willing to uphold the Catholic and Franciscan values of the University? Yes No * What is your overall GPA? 4.0 + 3.5 - 3.9 3.0 - 3.4 2.5 - 2.9 Below 2.5 * Please indicate your skill level with Microsoft Word & Excel, and Windows: Beginner Intermediate Advanced Expert I do not have experience using Microsoft Word or Excel, or Windows * Are you able to lift up to 30 lbs. with or without an accommodation? Yes No * Please indicate your office administrative or secretarial support experience: Less than 1 year 1 - 4 years 5 - 7 years 7 + years The Annual Security & Fire Safety Report is published in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act. Clery - 2021 University of St. Francis Annual Security and Fire Safety Report A paper copy of this report is available by contacting the Safety & Security office at 815-740-3200. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://stfrancis.peopleadmin.com/postings/5882": {"title": "Director of Community Engagement", "description": "University of St. Francis Employment Opportunities | Director of Community Engagement Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help USF Website About Us Saints Stats Mission & History USF is Nationally Ranked Leadership Take a Virtual Tour USF Alumni & Family Relations Notice of Nondiscrimination Director of Community Engagement Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to\u00a0bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. \u00a0If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Job Title Director of Community Engagement Position Number 005029 Department University Advancement - Joliet IL Job Grade 11 Anticipated Salary Range $60,500 - $66,000 Benefits https://stfrancis.edu/employment/ Notice of Nondiscrimination The University of St. Francis does not discriminate in its employment practices or in its educational programs on the basis of any protected class. The University also prohibits retaliation against any person opposing discrimination or harassment or participating in any internal or external investigation or complaint process related to allegations of misconduct. For a complete copy of USF\u2019s Policy on Equal Opportunity, Harassment, and Nondiscrimination for All Faculty, Students, Employees and Third Parties or for more information, please go to https://www.stfrancis.edu/titleix/ or contact the Title IX Coordinator at TitleIX@stfrancis.edu. Position Summary The Director of Community Engagement reports to the Chief Development Officer and is part of the University Advancement Division. This position directs the operations and planning of community relations as it pertains to the university, including communications, publications, special events, community relations and engagement and other related activities. This is a full-time, exempt position. Essential Duties & Responsibilities Serve as liaison and resource to all media representatives; pitches feature and news ideas; prepares campus representatives for media coverage; and writes and places press releases Serve as the liaison for strategic community partnerships (i.e. CAPA , Chambers of Commerce, community organizations, corporations and businesses) Establish, nurture and maintain positive external relationships with individuals, businesses and organizations that support the university\u2019s outreach efforts Support community partnerships through strategic sponsorships Lead efforts to represent the university favorably to the surrounding community, and attend community events Collaborate with other departments on community events and messaging Serve on the Crisis Management Team, complete National Incident Management System ( NIMS ) training and serve with the Chief Development Officer as a Public Information Officer ( PIO ) Plan and coordinate all relevant activities for university community events including Ambassador Day; assist with Caritas as necessary Develop and maintain Community Relations piece of the website including faculty experts and USF in the News Identify mechanisms to measure direct and indirect impact of community relations initiatives on engagement, strategic objectives, and brand enhancement Review, maintain and evaluate community and government relations budget Participate in University Advancement divisional projects that contribute to the university\u2019s culture, strategic vision and achievement of goals Interact with existing and potential donors, including scholarship donors Donor research and identification Donor gift recognition outreach activities Other duties as necessary Minimum Requirements Minimum three years related experience: journalism, English, public relations, media relations, community engagement, or marketing Bachelor\u2019s degree in a related field Ability to perform the physical requirements of the position Event planning experience Willingness to support the Catholic and Franciscan values of the university Preferred Requirements Master\u2019s degree in related field Hours/Shift/Work Schedule 40 hours/week, Monday through Friday, primarily days. Occasional evening and weekend work as needed for meetings and events. Physical Requirements of Position Work is performed in an office setting with minimal exposure to health or safety hazards. Substantial time is spent working on a computer. This is sedentary work which requires the following physical activities: sitting, walking, bending, stooping, finger dexterity, repetitive motions, talking, hearing and visual acuity. Posting Detail Information Posting Number FP0804-16 Open Date 09/14/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you willing to uphold the Catholic and Franciscan values of the University? Yes No * Will you now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status (e.g., H-1B visa status)? Yes No * Do you meet or exceed the minimum requirements outlined in this job posting? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Transcripts (unofficial are acceptable at time of application) Mission Response at https://pa-hrsuite-production.s3.amazonaws.com/856/docs/67939.pdf Optional Documents Letter of Recommendation 1 (you must upload something; letter writers may  send directly to Working@stfrancis.edu) Letter of Recommendation 2 (you must upload something; letter writers may  send directly to Working@stfrancis.edu) The Annual Security & Fire Safety Report is published in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act. Clery - 2021 University of St. Francis Annual Security and Fire Safety Report A paper copy of this report is available by contacting the Safety & Security office at 815-740-3200. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://stfrancis.peopleadmin.com/postings/5881": {"title": "Chief Development Officer", "description": "University of St. Francis Employment Opportunities | Chief Development Officer Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help USF Website About Us Saints Stats Mission & History USF is Nationally Ranked Leadership Take a Virtual Tour USF Alumni & Family Relations Notice of Nondiscrimination Chief Development Officer Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to\u00a0bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. \u00a0If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The University of St. Francis invites applications for Chief Development Officer. Reporting directly to the university president, this position serves as the senior administration officer to provide strategic leadership and direction for all university fundraising activities. Primary duties include advancement-related research and planning, major gift requests, university stewardship activities, donor and alumni relations, leadership of annual giving programs, and donor data management. Applicants must demonstrate familiarity with the University's Catholic and Franciscan identity, and be committed to building collaborative partnerships with internal and external university constituencies. Review of applications begins immediately, though all applications received prior to September 28 are preferred. Applications must include a cover letter, resume, and list of three references. Any questions may be directed to search committee chair Brian Dilger at bdilger@stfrancis.edu . Position Details Position Information Job Title Chief Development Officer Position Number 005000 Department University Advancement - Joliet IL Job Grade 17 Anticipated Salary Range $130,000-$140,000 Benefits stfrancis.edu/employment Notice of Nondiscrimination The University of St. Francis does not discriminate in its employment practices or in its educational programs on the basis of any protected class. The University also prohibits retaliation against any person opposing discrimination or harassment or participating in any internal or external investigation or complaint process related to allegations of misconduct. For a complete copy of USF\u2019s Policy on Equal Opportunity, Harassment, and Nondiscrimination for All Faculty, Students, Employees and Third Parties or for more information, please go to https://www.stfrancis.edu/titleix/ or contact the Title IX Coordinator at TitleIX@stfrancis.edu. Position Summary The Chief Development Officer ( CDO ) is responsible for developing, implementing, and overseeing a comprehensive, multi-year, data-driven fundraising strategy aligned with the organization\u2019s mission. Reporting to the President, CDO is tasked with identifying philanthropic supporters to expand contributions from private financial support. COLLABORATIVE NATURE OF POSITION The success of philanthropy relies heavily on effective, university- and community-wide collaboration \u2013 including the Board of Trustees, alumni, senior administration, university athletics, students, faculty, alumni in general, and members of civil society (non-profit and for-profit businesses and governmental bodies) to access the needs and outcomes of the University. The CDO will instill a culture of philanthropy throughout the organization and in the community with a broad base of meaningful engagement opportunities to encourage constituencies to investment in and support the University. REPORTING RELATIONSHIPS The Chief Development Officer reports to the President of the University and serves on the Executive Council. The alumni, advancement, and external relations functions report to the CDO , which presently include the following direct reports: Assistant Director of Advancement and Alumni Relations Assistant Director of Scholarships and Community Relations Donor Engagement and Giving Manager University Advancement Development Associate Others, as defined. Essential Duties & Responsibilities Serve as the chief advisor to the President on all matters related to institutional advancement. Develop, coordinate, and execute long- and short-term funding strategies in collaboration with faculty and administration including annual giving, online and direct marketing campaigns, major gifts, special events, and other solicitations. Set goals and benchmarks based on industry best practices that support the mission focus and measure the department employees\u2019 accomplishments, individually and collectively. Oversee the enhancement of alumni relations and support new efforts to engage and renew relationships. Seek and cultivate new corporate partnerships to enhance the mission and services of the University. Prepares, recommends, and implements budgets for assigned areas, monitors expenditures, and assures that human and financial resources are allocated efficiently and effectively. Actively and effectively engage with Trustees, alumni, and other key volunteers to identify and request financial support and involvement, which may entail some travel. Link constituent relationship management efforts to institutionalize donor data and preferences. Directly manage a portfolio of 20-30 (non-Trustee) donors giving $10,000+ annually. Support the President in managing his or her portfolio of donors \u2013 including Trustees. Maintain in-depth knowledge of the University\u2019s distinctive history, mission and philosophy, and program offerings. Serve as and/or support the University\u2019s spokesperson for select media inquiries as assigned. Provide managerial leadership of and strategic direction to the Advancement office. Adhere to the highest ethical standards; convey a professional and positive demeanor; and lead division in ongoing professional development. Manage all resources required for division programs and initiatives. Demonstrate a commitment to continuous improvement. Minimum Requirements Bachelor\u2019s degree in relevant/related field. Five years+ of successful fundraising and external relations leadership experience. In-depth working knowledge of and experience with best practices related to fund development and prospective donor identification. Significant experience in major gift solicitation. Ability to organize and oversee special events sponsored by the University as part of its expanded fundraising goals. Management style supportive of building respectful and collaborative relationships with all members of the campus community. Ability to actively participate in campus, Joliet, and Will County communities where opportunities to represent the university to prospective donors and friends exist. Willingness to support the Catholic and Franciscan values of the University. Excellent verbal and written communication skills. Mastery of data and standard technology programs (e.g. Microsoft Office). Ability to perform the physical requirements of the position. Preferred Requirements Experience in successful fundraising and external relations in higher education. Experience with Banner. 10 years\u2019 experience in university advancement. Hours/Shift/Work Schedule Full-time exempt position, it is expected that work will be performed to completion. Minimum of 40 hours per week, days, Monday through Friday; evening and/or weekend hours as needed. Physical Requirements of Position Work is performed in an office setting with minimal exposure to health or safety hazards. Substantial time is spent working on a computer, local and national travel and meeting with individuals in a variety of settings. Posting Detail Information Posting Number FP0801-16 Open Date 08/31/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you willing to uphold the Catholic and Franciscan values of the University? Yes No * Will you now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status (e.g., H-1B visa status)? Yes No * Do you have or exceed the minimum qualifications as listed in this posting? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Transcripts (unofficial are acceptable at time of application) Mission Response at https://pa-hrsuite-production.s3.amazonaws.com/856/docs/67939.pdf Optional Documents Letter of Recommendation 1 (you must upload something; letter writers may  send directly to Working@stfrancis.edu) Letter of Recommendation 2 (you must upload something; letter writers may  send directly to Working@stfrancis.edu) The Annual Security & Fire Safety Report is published in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act. Clery - 2021 University of St. Francis Annual Security and Fire Safety Report A paper copy of this report is available by contacting the Safety & Security office at 815-740-3200. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://stfrancis.peopleadmin.com/postings/5879": {"title": "Microbiology Adjunct Faculty Spring 2027", "description": "University of St. Francis Employment Opportunities | Microbiology Adjunct Faculty Spring 2027 Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help USF Website About Us Saints Stats Mission & History USF is Nationally Ranked Leadership Take a Virtual Tour USF Alumni & Family Relations Notice of Nondiscrimination Microbiology Adjunct Faculty Spring 2027 Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to\u00a0bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. \u00a0If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This is a part-time position located in Joliet, Illinois, USA, and is available for the Spring 2027 semester. We are an equal opportunity employer and welcome all persons. Position Details Position Information Job Title Microbiology Adjunct Faculty Spring 2027 Position Number FAXXXX-00 Department Natural Sciences Adjunct Faculty - Joliet, IL Job Grade Anticipated Salary Range $905 - $930 per credit hour Benefits Not Benefits Eligible Notice of Nondiscrimination The University of St. Francis does not discriminate in its employment practices or in its educational programs on the basis of any protected class. The University also prohibits retaliation against any person opposing discrimination or harassment or participating in any internal or external investigation or complaint process related to allegations of misconduct. For a complete copy of USF\u2019s Policy on Equal Opportunity, Harassment, and Nondiscrimination for All Faculty, Students, Employees and Third Parties or for more information, please go to https://www.stfrancis.edu/titleix/ or contact the Title IX Coordinator at TitleIX@stfrancis.edu. Position Summary Teach microbiology courses (lecture and/or lab) from January 11, 2027 \u2013 May 7, 2027. The University of St. Francis is a welcoming community of learners committed to enhancing diversity and equity. Essential Duties & Responsibilities Adjuncts are responsible for course planning and instruction. In addition, adjunct faculty are responsible for student evaluation, and timely and accurate submission of required paperwork related to instruction. Minimum Requirements \u2022 Master of Science degree in related field \u2022 Ability to perform the physical requirements of the position \u2022 Willingness to support the Catholic and Franciscan values of the university Preferred Requirements \u2022 Prior experience teaching microbiology courses at the college-level \u2022 Available to teach during the day (8am-5pm) \u2022 Doctoral degree in related field Hours/Shift/Work Schedule There is some flexibility based on availability; courses could be taught during the day (preferred) or evenings. All class are face-to-face with online support, and laboratories include hands-on and inquiry-based components. Physical Requirements of Position Work is performed in classroom and laboratory settings with minimal exposure to health or safety hazards. Substantial time is spent working on a computer. This is sedentary work which requires the following physical activities: sitting, walking, bending, stooping, finger dexterity, repetitive motions, talking, hearing and visual acuity. Posting Detail Information Posting Number FP0802-16 Open Date 09/11/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other * Are you willing to uphold the Catholic and Franciscan values of the University? Yes No * Please indicate your highest level of education: Less than GED/high school diploma GED/high school diploma Bachelor's degree Master's degree In a doctoral program ABD Doctorate * How many years of relevant experience do you have? Less than 1 year 1 - 2 years 3 - 4 years 5 - 7 years More than 7 years * Are you available to teach classes on weekdays - either during the daytime or evening - at the Joliet campus? Yes No * Please indicate your teaching experience in higher education: Less than 1 year 1-3 years 4 + years * Will you now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status (e.g., H-1B visa status)? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Transcripts (unofficial are acceptable at time of application) Mission Response at https://pa-hrsuite-production.s3.amazonaws.com/856/docs/67939.pdf Optional Documents Letter of Recommendation 1 (you must upload something; letter writers may  send directly to Working@stfrancis.edu) Letter of Recommendation 2 (you must upload something; letter writers may  send directly to Working@stfrancis.edu) The Annual Security & Fire Safety Report is published in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act. Clery - 2021 University of St. Francis Annual Security and Fire Safety Report A paper copy of this report is available by contacting the Safety & Security office at 815-740-3200. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://stfrancis.peopleadmin.com/postings/5878": {"title": "Assistant Men&#39;s Basketball Coach - Part-Time", "description": "University of St. Francis Employment Opportunities | Assistant Men&#39;s Basketball Coach - Part-Time Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help USF Website About Us Saints Stats Mission & History USF is Nationally Ranked Leadership Take a Virtual Tour USF Alumni & Family Relations Notice of Nondiscrimination Assistant Men's Basketball Coach - Part-Time Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to\u00a0bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. \u00a0If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Job Title Assistant Men's Basketball Coach - Part-Time Position Number 006826-00 Department Athletics: Joliet Job Grade Anticipated Salary Range $2,000 Benefits Not Benefit Eligible Notice of Nondiscrimination The University of St. Francis does not discriminate in its employment practices or in its educational programs on the basis of any protected class. The University also prohibits retaliation against any person opposing discrimination or harassment or participating in any internal or external investigation or complaint process related to allegations of misconduct. For a complete copy of USF\u2019s Policy on Equal Opportunity, Harassment, and Nondiscrimination for All Faculty, Students, Employees and Third Parties or for more information, please go to https://www.stfrancis.edu/titleix/ or contact the Title IX Coordinator at TitleIX@stfrancis.edu. Position Summary Assist the head men\u2019s basketball coach in coaching and leadership aspects of a model men\u2019s basketball program as they relate to academic commitment, supervision of staff and personnel, practice organization and instruction, game preparation and recruitment. Essential Duties & Responsibilities \u2022 Demonstrate respect for the Catholic and Franciscan values of the university. \u2022 Demonstrate the ability to relate effectively to student-athletes, coaches, staff, administration and the University community. \u2022 Participate in and promote a culture of continuing quality improvement. \u2022 Assumption of coaching responsibilities related to the sport of men\u2019s basketball. \u2022 Provision of assistance in certain administrative responsibilities related to the sport of men\u2019s basketball. \u2022 Provision of assistance in monitoring the academic progress of student-athletes. \u2022 Provision of assistance in the enforcement of team rules. \u2022 Provision of assistance in the planning, development and conducting of all in-season and off-season practices and conditioning sessions. \u2022 Provision of assistance in the instruction of staff. \u2022 Ensure that proper safety guidelines and standards are maintained. \u2022 Coordinate certain strategy related to the sport of men\u2019s basketball. \u2022 Responsible for certain aspects of recruitment in accordance with university and NAIA rules. \u2022 Understanding and support of all athletic policies and regulations, as well as all philosophies, of the University, Chicagoland Collegiate Athletic Conference and National Association of Intercollegiate Athletics. \u2022 Understanding and support of the NAIA Champions of Character Coaches Code. \u2022 Represent the athletic department and university in a professional manner at various internal and external functions and in working with internal and external constituencies, including but not limited to the media and general public. \u2022 Perform other administrative duties within the department as assigned. \u2022 Must be able to work nights, weekends and holidays. Minimum Requirements \u2022 High school diploma or GED . \u2022 Three years of basketball playing or coaching experience. \u2022 Ability to perform the physical requirements of the position. \u2022 Ability and willingness to work nights, weekends and holidays. \u2022 Willingness to support the Catholic and Franciscan values of the University. Preferred Requirements \u2022 Bachelor\u2019s degree. \u2022 Three years of collegiate basketball coaching experience. Hours/Shift/Work Schedule Hours vary, but do include weekends, nights and holidays. Physical Requirements of Position Work is performed in both an office setting and at athletic arenas with moderate exposure to varying weather conditions, but minimal health or safety hazards. Substantial time is spent working on a computer. This is sedentary work, which requires the following physical activities: sitting, walking, bending, stooping, finger dexterity, repetitive motions, talking, hearing and visual acuity. Travel is required. Hours of work include some nights, weekends and may include working up to 12 hours a day. Posting Detail Information Posting Number FP0803-16 Open Date 09/10/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other * Are you willing to uphold the Catholic and Franciscan values of the University? Yes No * Please indicate your highest level of education: Less than GED/high school diploma GED/high school diploma Bachelor's degree Master's degree In a doctoral program ABD Doctorate * Please indicate your basketball playing/coaching experience: Less than 3 years 3 - 4 years 5 + years * Are you able to perform the physical requirements of the position, with or without accommodation? Yes No * Are you available and willing to work weekends, nights and holidays? Yes No * Will you now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status (e.g., H-1B visa status)? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Mission Response at https://pa-hrsuite-production.s3.amazonaws.com/856/docs/67939.pdf Resume Optional Documents Transcripts (unofficial are acceptable at time of application) The Annual Security & Fire Safety Report is published in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act. Clery - 2021 University of St. Francis Annual Security and Fire Safety Report A paper copy of this report is available by contacting the Safety & Security office at 815-740-3200. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://stfrancis.peopleadmin.com/postings/5876": {"title": "Student Layout Designer", "description": "University of St. Francis Employment Opportunities | Student Layout Designer Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help USF Website About Us Saints Stats Mission & History USF is Nationally Ranked Leadership Take a Virtual Tour USF Alumni & Family Relations Notice of Nondiscrimination Student Layout Designer Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to\u00a0bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. \u00a0If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Send offline application to Brien McHugh S402 Posting Information First Section Job Title Student Layout Designer Position Number ST3243-00 Organizational Unit Encounter Student Workers Posting Number SP0943-16 Notice of Nondiscrimination The University of St. Francis does not discriminate in its employment practices or in its educational programs on the basis of any protected class. The University also prohibits retaliation against any person opposing discrimination or harassment or participating in any internal or external investigation or complaint process related to allegations of misconduct. For a complete copy of USF\u2019s Policy on Equal Opportunity, Harassment, and Nondiscrimination for All Faculty, Students, Employees and Third Parties or for more information, please go to https://www.stfrancis.edu/titleix/ or contact the Title IX Coordinator at TitleIX@stfrancis.edu. Requirements Responsibilities Design layouts for the Encounter Student News Magazine (Technology, Critical Thinking, Professionalism) Qualifications Current USF student in good standing Must be familiar with Adobe Creative Suite, especially In Design for page layout (Technology, Critical Thinking, Professionalism) Federal Work Study eligibility preferred Pay Rate Hourly $17.00 Benefits Not Benefit Eligibile Hours / Week 5 Close Date 09/30/2026 Quick Link https://stfrancis.peopleadmin.com/postings/5872 Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently enrolled at USF as either a full-time undergrad or a part-time graduate student, and in good standing? Yes No * Do you have expe