e University of St. Francis does not discriminate in its employment practices or in its educational programs on the basis of any protected class. The University also prohibits retaliation against any person opposing discrimination or harassment or participating in any internal or external investigation or complaint process related to allegations of misconduct. For a complete copy of USF\u2019s Policy on Equal Opportunity, Harassment, and Nondiscrimination for All Faculty, Students, Employees and Third Parties or for more information, please go to https://www.stfrancis.edu/titleix/ or contact the Title IX Coordinator at TitleIX@stfrancis.edu. Requirements Responsibilities Online research and data entry; updating constituent records Maintaining registrations, invitation lists and prepare for advancement events/meetings. (Critical Thinking and Technology) Make thank you and reminder calls to donors. (Communication) Assist with maintenance of social media sites. ( Technology ) Clerical duties including: making copies, scanning, e-mailing, hanging signs, processing applications/registrations, and making/answering calls . (Professionalism) Organization and tracking of inventory. (Professionalism) Carry-out Advancement processes. (Professionalism) Other duties as assigned. Qualifications Proficient computer skills including knowledge of Microsoft Office programs Excellent communication skills both written and oral Experience using social media as a marketing tool Strong organizational skills Ability to maintain confidentiality Ability to multi-task and complete important projects within deadlines Must be dependable and punctual Ability to work year round including school break periods Current USF student, in good standing Preferred: freshman or sophomore standing Pay Rate Hourly $15.00/hour Benefits Not benefit-eligible. Hours / Week 10 hours per week Close Date 11/01/2025 Quick Link https://stfrancis.peopleadmin.com/postings/5864 Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently enrolled at USF as either a full-time undergrad or a part-time graduate student, and in good standing? Yes No * Are you eligible for the Federal Work Study Award in your Financial Aid package? Yes No * Please indicate your skill level with Microsoft Word & Excel, and Windows: Beginner Intermediate Advanced Expert I do not have experience using Microsoft Word or Excel, or Windows * Are you able and willing to work year-round, including during school break periods (spring, summer and fall)? Yes No * Are you willing to uphold the Catholic and Franciscan values of the University? Yes No The Annual Security & Fire Safety Report is published in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act. Clery - 2021 University of St. Francis Annual Security and Fire Safety Report A paper copy of this report is available by contacting the Safety & Security office at 815-740-3200. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://stfrancis.peopleadmin.com/postings/5863": {"title": "Athletic Department Student Worker", "description": "University of St. Francis Employment Opportunities | Athletic Department Student Worker Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help USF Website About Us Saints Stats Mission & History USF is Nationally Ranked Leadership Take a Virtual Tour USF Alumni & Family Relations Notice of Nondiscrimination Athletic Department Student Worker Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to\u00a0bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. \u00a0If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information First Section Job Title Athletic Department Student Worker Position Number ST6810-00 Organizational Unit Athletics- Student Workers- Joliet, IL Posting Number Notice of Nondiscrimination The University of St. Francis does not discriminate in its employment practices or in its educational programs on the basis of any protected class. The University also prohibits retaliation against any person opposing discrimination or harassment or participating in any internal or external investigation or complaint process related to allegations of misconduct. For a complete copy of USF\u2019s Policy on Equal Opportunity, Harassment, and Nondiscrimination for All Faculty, Students, Employees and Third Parties or for more information, please go to https://www.stfrancis.edu/titleix/ or contact the Title IX Coordinator at TitleIX@stfrancis.edu. Requirements Responsibilities Provides support to the USF athletic department in the form of various game management responsibilities and/or a fitness center attendant. (Professionalism and Leadership) Qualifications Must be a current USF student in good academic standing. Must be available to work weekends and evenings. Pay Rate Hourly $15.00 Benefits Not Benefit-eligible Hours / Week Up to 20 hours/week Close Date Quick Link https://stfrancis.peopleadmin.com/postings/5829 Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). The Annual Security & Fire Safety Report is published in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act. Clery - 2021 University of St. Francis Annual Security and Fire Safety Report A paper copy of this report is available by contacting the Safety & Security office at 815-740-3200. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://stfrancis.peopleadmin.com/postings/5858": {"title": "Academic Affairs Student Worker", "description": "University of St. Francis Employment Opportunities | Academic Affairs Student Worker Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help USF Website About Us Saints Stats Mission & History USF is Nationally Ranked Leadership Take a Virtual Tour USF Alumni & Family Relations Notice of Nondiscrimination Academic Affairs Student Worker Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to\u00a0bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. \u00a0If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Experience with Microsoft Word and Excel Posting Information First Section Job Title Academic Affairs Student Worker Position Number ST3220-01 Organizational Unit Office of the Provost Posting Number SP0940-16 Notice of Nondiscrimination The University of St. Francis does not discriminate in its employment practices or in its educational programs on the basis of any protected class. The University also prohibits retaliation against any person opposing discrimination or harassment or participating in any internal or external investigation or complaint process related to allegations of misconduct. For a complete copy of USF\u2019s Policy on Equal Opportunity, Harassment, and Nondiscrimination for All Faculty, Students, Employees and Third Parties or for more information, please go to https://www.stfrancis.edu/titleix/ or contact the Title IX Coordinator at TitleIX@stfrancis.edu. Requirements Responsibilities The Student Worker provides administrative, organizational, project, and day-to-day operational support for the department of Academic Affairs.\u00a0 This position requires good communication and organizational skills, proficient computer skills, and the ability to work independently and collaboratively on a variety of projects. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Communicate professionally with students, faculty, staff, and external stakeholders through email, phone, virtual platforms, and in-person interactions. Administrative duties associated with Academic Affairs (copying, scanning, filing, sorting, etc.).\u00a0 (Professionalism, Technology) Assist with planning, coordinating, and implementing departmental projects and special initiatives.\u00a0 (Teamwork, Leadership, Critical Thinking) Track project timelines, update status reports, and support project deliverables as assigned. (Teamwork, Communication, Professionalism) Support student retention efforts by assisting with outreach campaigns, follow-up communications, student engagement activities, and resource referrals. (Communication, Critical Thinking, Technology) Monitor and update databases, spreadsheets, and tracking systems to ensure data accuracy. (Professionalism and Technology) Work independently to prioritize assignments, manage deadlines, and complete tasks with minimal supervision. (Professionalism) Maintain confidentiality of student and departmental information in accordance with institutional policies. (Professionalism) Other duties as assigned Qualifications Qualifications: Current USF student in good standing. Proficient computer skills including knowledge of Microsoft Office programs. Good communication skills, both written and oral. Strong organizational and time-management abilities. Ability to work independently with minimal supervision. Attention to detail and commitment to accuracy. Ability to maintain confidentiality. Good problem solving and critical thinking skills. Pay Rate Hourly $15.00 Benefits Not Benefits-Eligible Hours / Week 10-20 Close Date Quick Link https://stfrancis.peopleadmin.com/postings/5857 Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently enrolled at USF as either a full-time undergrad or a part-time graduate student, and in good standing? Yes No * Are you eligible for the Federal Work Study Award in your Financial Aid package? Yes No * Are you willing to uphold the Catholic and Franciscan values of the University? Yes No The Annual Security & Fire Safety Report is published in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act. Clery - 2021 University of St. Francis Annual Security and Fire Safety Report A paper copy of this report is available by contacting the Safety & Security office at 815-740-3200. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://stfrancis.peopleadmin.com/postings/5856": {"title": "Assistant Baseball Coach - Part-Time", "description": "University of St. Francis Employment Opportunities | Assistant Baseball Coach - Part-Time Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help USF Website About Us Saints Stats Mission & History USF is Nationally Ranked Leadership Take a Virtual Tour USF Alumni & Family Relations Notice of Nondiscrimination Assistant Baseball Coach - Part-Time Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to\u00a0bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. \u00a0If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Job Title Assistant Baseball Coach - Part-Time Position Number XXXXXX-XX Department Athletics: Joliet Job Grade N/A Anticipated Salary Range $1,000-$3,000 Benefits Not- Benefits Eligible Notice of Nondiscrimination The University of St. Francis does not discriminate in its employment practices or in its educational programs on the basis of any protected class. The University also prohibits retaliation against any person opposing discrimination or harassment or participating in any internal or external investigation or complaint process related to allegations of misconduct. For a complete copy of USF\u2019s Policy on Equal Opportunity, Harassment, and Nondiscrimination for All Faculty, Students, Employees and Third Parties or for more information, please go to https://www.stfrancis.edu/titleix/ or contact the Title IX Coordinator at TitleIX@stfrancis.edu. Position Summary Assist the head baseball coach in coaching and leadership aspects of a model baseball program as they relate to academic commitment, supervision of staff and personnel, practice organization and instruction, game preparation and recruitment. Essential Duties & Responsibilities Demonstrate respect for the Catholic and Franciscan values of the university. Demonstrate the ability to relate effectively to student-athletes, coaches, staff, administration and the University community. Participate in and promote a culture of continuing quality improvement. Assumption of coaching responsibilities related to the sport of baseball. Provision of assistance in certain administrative responsibilities related to the sport of baseball. Provision of assistance in monitoring the academic progress of student-athletes. Provision of assistance in the enforcement of team rules. Provision of assistance in the planning, development and conducting of all in-season and off-season practices and conditioning sessions. Provision of assistance in the instruction of staff. Ensure that proper safety guidelines and standards are maintained. Coordinate certain strategy related to the sport of baseball. Responsible for certain aspects of recruitment in accordance with university and NAIA rules. Understanding and support of all athletic policies and regulations, as well as all philosophies, of the University, Chicagoland Collegiate Athletic Conference and National Association of Intercollegiate Athletics. Understanding and support of the NAIA Champions of Character Coaches Code. Represent the athletic department and university in a professional manner at various internal and external functions and in working with internal and external constituencies, including but not limited to the media and general public. Perform other administrative duties within the department as assigned. Must be able to work nights, weekends and holidays. Minimum Requirements High school diploma or GED . Three years of baseball playing or coaching experience. Ability to perform the physical requirements of the position. Ability and willingness to work nights, weekends and holidays. Willingness to support the Catholic and Franciscan values of the University. Preferred Requirements Bachelor\u2019s degree. Three years of collegiate baseball coaching experience. Hours/Shift/Work Schedule Hours vary, but do include weekends, nights and holidays. Physical Requirements of Position Work is performed in both an office setting and at athletic arenas with moderate exposure to varying weather conditions, but minimal health or safety hazards. Substantial time is spent working on a computer. This is sedentary work, which requires the following physical activities: sitting, walking, bending, stooping, finger dexterity, repetitive motions, talking, hearing and visual acuity. Travel is required. Hours of work include some nights, weekends and may include working up to 12 hours a day. Posting Detail Information Posting Number FP0799-16 Open Date 08/24/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you willing to uphold the Catholic and Franciscan values of the University? Yes No * Will you now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status (e.g., H-1B visa status)? Yes No * Please indicate your highest level of education: Less than high school diploma/GED High school diploma/GED Associate's degree or post-secondary training/certificate program Bachelor's degree Master's degree In a doctoral program ABD Doctorate * Are you available and willing to work weekends, nights and holidays? Yes No * Please indicate your highest level of experience as a softball player/coach: Less than 3 years 3 - 5 years 5+ years I have collegiate softball coaching experience Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Mission Response at https://pa-hrsuite-production.s3.amazonaws.com/856/docs/67939.pdf Optional Documents Cover Letter Transcripts (unofficial are acceptable at time of application) Letter of Recommendation 1 (you must upload something; letter writers may  send directly to Working@stfrancis.edu) Letter of Recommendation 2 (you must upload something; letter writers may  send directly to Working@stfrancis.edu) License/Certification The Annual Security & Fire Safety Report is published in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act. Clery - 2021 University of St. Francis Annual Security and Fire Safety Report A paper copy of this report is available by contacting the Safety & Security office at 815-740-3200. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://stfrancis.peopleadmin.com/postings/5851": {"title": "Career Success Center Student Worker", "description": "University of St. Francis Employment Opportunities | Career Success Center Student Worker Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help USF Website About Us Saints Stats Mission & History USF is Nationally Ranked Leadership Take a Virtual Tour USF Alumni & Family Relations Notice of Nondiscrimination Career Success Center Student Worker Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to\u00a0bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. \u00a0If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information First Section Job Title Career Success Center Student Worker Position Number ST3630-00 Organizational Unit Career Success Student Workers - Joliet, IL Posting Number SP0939-16 Notice of Nondiscrimination The University of St. Francis does not discriminate in its employment practices or in its educational programs on the basis of any protected class. The University also prohibits retaliation against any person opposing discrimination or harassment or participating in any internal or external investigation or complaint process related to allegations of misconduct. For a complete copy of USF\u2019s Policy on Equal Opportunity, Harassment, and Nondiscrimination for All Faculty, Students, Employees and Third Parties or for more information, please go to https://www.stfrancis.edu/titleix/ or contact the Title IX Coordinator at TitleIX@stfrancis.edu. Requirements Responsibilities Responsibilities Assist with center marketing for events and services, ability to create promotional materials using design programs, or willingness to train. ( Communication and Technology ) Conduct research on careers by major and coordinate information with Career Success Team. ( Teamwork and Critical Thinking ) Speak to businesses about possible internship placement sites. Help review resumes. ( Communication ) Update social media pages, contribute and write for Center\u2019s Blog Page. ( Technology ) Provide presentations to groups. ( Communication and Leadership ) Call outside contacts when necessary, including recent graduates, and employers. ( Communication ) Work at Career Success Center events. ( Professionalism ) Qualifications Current USF Student in good standing Federal Work Study Eligible Preferred Strong organizational skills Pay Rate Hourly 15.00 Benefits Not benefit-eligible Hours / Week 6-12 hours Close Date 01/30/2026 Quick Link https://stfrancis.peopleadmin.com/postings/5850 Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you willing to uphold the Catholic and Franciscan values of the University? Yes No * Are you eligible for the Federal Work Study Award in your Financial Aid package? Yes No * Are you currently enrolled at USF as either a full-time undergrad or a part-time graduate student, and in good standing? Yes No * Please explain your overall experience using LinkedIn (Do you currently have a LinkedIn profile? How often do you access LinkedIn? How/why do you utilize or engage with content on LinkedIn?). (Open Ended Question) The Annual Security & Fire Safety Report is published in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act. Clery - 2021 University of St. Francis Annual Security and Fire Safety Report A paper copy of this report is available by contacting the Safety & Security office at 815-740-3200. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://stfrancis.peopleadmin.com/postings/5839": {"title": "Assistant Men&#39;s Volleyball Coach - Part-Time", "description": "University of St. Francis Employment Opportunities | Assistant Men&#39;s Volleyball Coach - Part-Time Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help USF Website About Us Saints Stats Mission & History USF is Nationally Ranked Leadership Take a Virtual Tour USF Alumni & Family Relations Notice of Nondiscrimination Assistant Men's Volleyball Coach - Part-Time Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to\u00a0bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. \u00a0If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Job Title Assistant Men's Volleyball Coach - Part-Time Position Number 006852-00 Department Athletics: Joliet Job Grade Anticipated Salary Range $1,000-$5,000 Benefits Not Benefit-Eligible Notice of Nondiscrimination The University of St. Francis does not discriminate in its employment practices or in its educational programs on the basis of any protected class. The University also prohibits retaliation against any person opposing discrimination or harassment or participating in any internal or external investigation or complaint process related to allegations of misconduct. For a complete copy of USF\u2019s Policy on Equal Opportunity, Harassment, and Nondiscrimination for All Faculty, Students, Employees and Third Parties or for more information, please go to https://www.stfrancis.edu/titleix/ or contact the Title IX Coordinator at TitleIX@stfrancis.edu. Position Summary Assist the head men\u2019s volleyball coach in coaching and leadership aspects of a model men\u2019s volleyball program as they relate to academic commitment, supervision of staff and personnel, practice organization and instruction, meet preparation and recruitment. Essential Duties & Responsibilities Demonstrate respect for the Catholic and Franciscan values of the university. Demonstrate the ability to relate effectively to student-athletes, coaches, staff, administration and the University community. Participate in and promote a culture of continuing quality improvement. Assumption of coaching responsibilities related to the sport of men\u2019s volleyball. Provision of assistance in certain administrative responsibilities related to the sport of men\u2019s volleyball; in monitoring the academic progress of student-athletes; in the enforcement of team rules; in the planning, development and conducting of all in-season and off-season practices and conditioning sessions; in the instruction of staff. Ensure that proper safety guidelines and standards are maintained. Coordinate certain strategy related to the sport of men\u2019s volleyball. Responsible for certain aspects of recruitment in accordance with university and NAIA rules. Understanding and support of all athletic policies and regulations, as well as all philosophies, of the University, Chicagoland Collegiate Athletic Conference and National Association of Intercollegiate Athletics. Understanding and support of the NAIA Champions of Character Coaches Code. Represent the athletic department and university in a professional manner at various internal and external functions and in working with internal and external constituencies, including but not limited to the media and general public. Perform other administrative duties within the department as assigned. Must be able to work nights, weekends and holidays. Minimum Requirements High school diploma or GED . Three years of volleyball athlete or coaching experience. Ability to perform the physical requirements of the position. Ability and willingness to work nights, weekends and holidays. Willingness to support the Catholic and Franciscan values of the University. Preferred Requirements Bachelor\u2019s degree. Three years of collegiate volleyball coaching experience. Hours/Shift/Work Schedule Hours vary, but do include weekends, nights and holidays. Physical Requirements of Position Work is performed in both an office setting and at athletic arenas with moderate exposure to varying weather conditions, but minimal health or safety hazards. Substantial time is spent working on a computer. This is sedentary work, which requires the following physical activities: sitting, walking, bending, stooping, finger dexterity, repetitive motions, talking, hearing and visual acuity. Travel is required. Hours of work include some nights, weekends and may include working up to 12 hours a day. Posting Detail Information Posting Number FP0791-16 Open Date 07/29/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other * Are you willing to uphold the Catholic and Franciscan values of the University? Yes No * Will you now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status (e.g., H-1B visa status)? Yes No * Please indicate your highest level of education: Less than GED/high school diploma GED/high school diploma Bachelor's degree Master's degree In a doctoral program ABD Doctorate * Are you available and willing to work weekends, nights and holidays? Yes No * Do you have experience as a Cross-Country/Track athlete or coach? Yes No * Please indicate your highest level of coaching experience in CC/Track & Field: Less than 3 years 3 - 5 years 5+ years I have at least 3 years of collegiate CC/Track & Field coaching experience Applicant Documents Required Documents Transcripts (unofficial are acceptable at time of application) Mission Response at https://pa-hrsuite-production.s3.amazonaws.com/856/docs/67939.pdf Resume Optional Documents The Annual Security & Fire Safety Report is published in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act. Clery - 2021 University of St. Francis Annual Security and Fire Safety Report A paper copy of this report is available by contacting the Safety & Security office at 815-740-3200. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://stfrancis.peopleadmin.com/postings/5838": {"title": "Assistant Football Coach - Part-Time", "description": "University of St. Francis Employment Opportunities | Assistant Football Coach - Part-Time Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help USF Website About Us Saints Stats Mission & History USF is Nationally Ranked Leadership Take a Virtual Tour USF Alumni & Family Relations Notice of Nondiscrimination Assistant Football Coach - Part-Time Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to\u00a0bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. \u00a0If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Job Title Assistant Football Coach - Part-Time Position Number 006826-00 Department Athletics: Joliet Job Grade Anticipated Salary Range $2,000-$10,000 Benefits Not Benefit- Eligible Notice of Nondiscrimination The University of St. Francis does not discriminate in its employment practices or in its educational programs on the basis of any protected class. The University also prohibits retaliation against any person opposing discrimination or harassment or participating in any internal or external investigation or complaint process related to allegations of misconduct. For a complete copy of USF\u2019s Policy on Equal Opportunity, Harassment, and Nondiscrimination for All Faculty, Students, Employees and Third Parties or for more information, please go to https://www.stfrancis.edu/titleix/ or contact the Title IX Coordinator at TitleIX@stfrancis.edu. Position Summary Assist the head football coach in coaching and leadership aspects of a model football program as they relate to academic commitment, supervision of staff and personnel, practice organization and instruction, game preparation and recruitment. Essential Duties & Responsibilities \u2022 Demonstrate respect for the Catholic and Franciscan values of the university. \u2022 Demonstrate the ability to relate effectively to student-athletes, coaches, staff, administration and the University community. \u2022 Participate in and promote a culture of continuing quality improvement. \u2022 Assumption of coaching responsibilities related to the sport of football. \u2022 Provision of assistance in certain administrative responsibilities related to the sport of football. \u2022 Provision of assistance in monitoring the academic progress of student-athletes. \u2022 Provision of assistance in the enforcement of team rules. \u2022 Provision of assistance in the planning, development and conducting of all in-season and off-season practices and conditioning sessions. \u2022 Provision of assistance in the instruction of staff. \u2022 Ensure that proper safety guidelines and standards are maintained. \u2022 Coordinate certain strategy related to the sport of football. \u2022 Responsible for certain aspects of recruitment in accordance with university and NAIA rules. \u2022 Understanding and support of all athletic policies and regulations, as well as all philosophies, of the University, Chicagoland Collegiate Athletic Conference and National Association of Intercollegiate Athletics. \u2022 Understanding and support of the NAIA Champions of Character Coaches Code. \u2022 Represent the athletic department and university in a professional manner at various internal and external functions and in working with internal and external constituencies, including but not limited to the media and general public. \u2022 Perform other administrative duties within the department as assigned. \u2022 Must be able to work nights, weekends and holidays. Minimum Requirements \u2022 High school diploma or GED . \u2022 One year of football playing or coaching experience. \u2022 Ability to perform the physical requirements of the position. \u2022 Ability and willingness to work nights, weekends and holidays. \u2022 Willingness to support the Catholic and Franciscan values of the University. Preferred Requirements \u2022 Bachelor\u2019s degree. \u2022 Three years of collegiate football coaching experience. Hours/Shift/Work Schedule Hours vary, but do include weekends, nights and holidays. Physical Requirements of Position Work is performed in both an office setting and at athletic arenas with moderate exposure to varying weather conditions, but minimal health or safety hazards. Substantial time is spent working on a computer. This is sedentary work, which requires the following physical activities: sitting, walking, bending, stooping, finger dexterity, repetitive motions, talking, hearing and visual acuity. Travel is required. Hours of work include some nights, weekends and may include working up to 12 hours a day. Posting Detail Information Posting Number FP0789-16 Open Date 07/27/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other * Are you willing to uphold the Catholic and Franciscan values of the University? Yes No * Please indicate your highest level of education: Less than GED/high school diploma GED/high school diploma Bachelor's degree Master's degree In a doctoral program ABD Doctorate * Please indicate your basketball playing/coaching experience: Less than 3 years 3 - 4 years 5 + years * Are you able to perform the physical requirements of the position, with or without accommodation? Yes No * Are you available and willing to work weekends, nights and holidays? Yes No * Will you now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status (e.g., H-1B visa status)? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Mission Response at https://pa-hrsuite-production.s3.amazonaws.com/856/docs/67939.pdf Resume Optional Documents Transcripts (unofficial are acceptable at time of application) The Annual Security & Fire Safety Report is published in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act. Clery - 2021 University of St. Francis Annual Security and Fire Safety Report A paper copy of this report is available by contacting the Safety & Security office at 815-740-3200. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://stfrancis.peopleadmin.com/postings/5834": {"title": "Biology Adjunct Faculty Fall 2026", "description": "University of St. Francis Employment Opportunities | Biology Adjunct Faculty Fall 2026 Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help USF Website About Us Saints Stats Mission & History USF is Nationally Ranked Leadership Take a Virtual Tour USF Alumni & Family Relations Notice of Nondiscrimination Biology Adjunct Faculty Fall 2026 Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to\u00a0bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. \u00a0If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This is a part-time position located in Joliet, Illinois, USA, and is available for the Fall 2026 semester. We are an equal opportunity employer and welcome all persons. Position Details Position Information Job Title Biology Adjunct Faculty Fall 2026 Position Number FAXXXX-00 Department Natural Sciences Adjunct Faculty - Joliet, IL Job Grade Anticipated Salary Range $905 - $930 per credit hour Benefits Not Benefits Eligible Notice of Nondiscrimination The University of St. Francis does not discriminate in its employment practices or in its educational programs on the basis of any protected class. The University also prohibits retaliation against any person opposing discrimination or harassment or participating in any internal or external investigation or complaint process related to allegations of misconduct. For a complete copy of USF\u2019s Policy on Equal Opportunity, Harassment, and Nondiscrimination for All Faculty, Students, Employees and Third Parties or for more information, please go to https://www.stfrancis.edu/titleix/ or contact the Title IX Coordinator at TitleIX@stfrancis.edu. Position Summary Teach biology courses (lecture and/or lab) from August 24, 2026 -December 18, 2026. The University of St. Francis is a welcoming community of learners committed to enhancing diversity and equity. Essential Duties & Responsibilities Adjuncts are responsible for course planning and instruction. In addition, adjunct faculty are responsible for student evaluation, and timely and accurate submission of required paperwork related to instruction. Minimum Requirements \u2022 Master of Science degree in related field \u2022 Ability to perform the physical requirements of the position \u2022 Willingness to support the Catholic and Franciscan values of the university Preferred Requirements \u2022 Prior experience teaching biology courses at the college-level \u2022 Available to teach during the day (8am-5pm) \u2022 Doctoral degree in related field Hours/Shift/Work Schedule There is some flexibility based on availability; courses could be taught during the day (preferred) or evenings. All class are face-to-face with online support, and laboratories include hands-on and inquiry-based components. Physical Requirements of Position Work is performed in classroom and laboratory settings with minimal exposure to health or safety hazards. Substantial time is spent working on a computer. This is sedentary work which requires the following physical activities: sitting, walking, bending, stooping, finger dexterity, repetitive motions, talking, hearing and visual acuity. Posting Detail Information Posting Number FP0793-16 Open Date 07/30/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other * Are you willing to uphold the Catholic and Franciscan values of the University? Yes No * Please indicate your highest level of education: Less than GED/high school diploma GED/high school diploma Bachelor's degree Master's degree In a doctoral program ABD Doctorate * How many years of relevant experience do you have? Less than 1 year 1 - 2 years 3 - 4 years 5 - 7 years More than 7 years * Are you available to teach classes on weekdays - either during the daytime or evening - at the Joliet campus? Yes No * Please indicate your teaching experience in higher education: Less than 1 year 1-3 years 4 + years * Will you now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status (e.g., H-1B visa status)? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Transcripts (unofficial are acceptable at time of application) Mission Response at https://pa-hrsuite-production.s3.amazonaws.com/856/docs/67939.pdf Optional Documents Letter of Recommendation 1 (you must upload something; letter writers may  send directly to Working@stfrancis.edu) Letter of Recommendation 2 (you must upload something; letter writers may  send directly to Working@stfrancis.edu) The Annual Security & Fire Safety Report is published in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act. Clery - 2021 University of St. Francis Annual Security and Fire Safety Report A paper copy of this report is available by contacting the Safety & Security office at 815-740-3200. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://stfrancis.peopleadmin.com/postings/5828": {"title": "Men&#39;s &amp; Women&#39;s Volleyball Graduate Assistant", "description": "University of St. Francis Employment Opportunities | Men&#39;s &amp; Women&#39;s Volleyball Graduate Assistant Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help USF Website About Us Saints Stats Mission & History USF is Nationally Ranked Leadership Take a Virtual Tour USF Alumni