end link. \u00a0If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information First Section Job Title Women's Basketball Graduate Assistant Position Number GA6882-00 Organizational Unit Athletics- Student Workers- Joliet, IL Posting Number SP0937-16 Notice of Nondiscrimination The University of St. Francis does not discriminate in its employment practices or in its educational programs on the basis of any protected class. The University also prohibits retaliation against any person opposing discrimination or harassment or participating in any internal or external investigation or complaint process related to allegations of misconduct. For a complete copy of USF\u2019s Policy on Equal Opportunity, Harassment, and Nondiscrimination for All Faculty, Students, Employees and Third Parties or for more information, please go to https://www.stfrancis.edu/titleix/ or contact the Title IX Coordinator at TitleIX@stfrancis.edu. Requirements Responsibilities \u2022 Demonstrate respect for the Catholic and Franciscan values of the university. \u2022 Demonstrate the ability to relate effectively to student-athletes, coaches, staff, administration and the University community. \u2022 Participate in and promote a culture of continuing quality improvement. \u2022 Assumption of coaching responsibilities related to the sport of basketball. \u2022 Assumption of certain administrative responsibilities related to the sport of basketball. \u2022 Provision of assistance in monitoring the academic progress of student-athletes. \u2022 Provision of assistance in the enforcement of team rules. \u2022 Provision of assistance in the planning, development and conducting of all in-season and off-season practices and conditioning sessions. \u2022 Ensure that proper safety guidelines and standards are maintained. \u2022 Coordinate certain strategy related to the sport of basketball. \u2022 Responsible for certain aspects of recruitment in accordance with university and NAIA rules. \u2022 Understanding and support of all athletic policies and regulations, as well as all philosophies, of the University of St. Francis, Chicagoland Collegiate Athletic Conference and National Association of Intercollegiate Athletics. \u2022 Understanding and support of NAIA Champions of Character Coaches Code. \u2022 Represent the athletic department and university in a professional manner at various internal and external functions and in working with internal and external constituencies, including but not limited to the media and general public. \u2022 Perform other administrative duties within the department as assigned. \u2022 Must be able to work nights, weekends and holidays. Qualifications \u2022 Bachelor\u2019s degree. \u2022 Acceptance into USF\u2019s masters program \u2022 Ability to perform the physical requirements of the position. \u2022 Ability and willingness to work nights, weekends and holidays. \u2022 Willingness to support the Catholic and Franciscan values of the University. Pay Rate Hourly $5,000 Stipend (up to 20 hours of work per week as needed) & Tuition Waiver (total graduate credits cannot exceed 18 graduate credit hours per academic year) Benefits Not Benefits-Eligible Hours / Week Varies based on basketball practice & game schedules; includes weekends, nights & holidays. Close Date Quick Link https://stfrancis.peopleadmin.com/postings/5818 Documents Required Documents Resume Transcripts (unofficial are acceptable at time of application) Mission Response at https://pa-hrsuite-production.s3.amazonaws.com/856/docs/67939.pdf Optional Documents Cover Letter Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you willing to uphold the Catholic and Franciscan values of the University? Yes No * Are you available and willing to work weekends, nights and holidays? Yes No * Are you currently accepted into an USF Master's program? Yes No The Annual Security & Fire Safety Report is published in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act. Clery - 2021 University of St. Francis Annual Security and Fire Safety Report A paper copy of this report is available by contacting the Safety & Security office at 815-740-3200. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://stfrancis.peopleadmin.com/postings/5809": {"title": "Assistant Men&#39;s and Women&#39;s CC/Track &amp; Field Coach - Part-Time", "description": "University of St. Francis Employment Opportunities | Assistant Men&#39;s and Women&#39;s CC/Track &amp; Field Coach - Part-Time Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help USF Website About Us Saints Stats Mission & History USF is Nationally Ranked Leadership Take a Virtual Tour USF Alumni & Family Relations Notice of Nondiscrimination Assistant Men's and Women's CC/Track & Field Coach - Part-Time Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to\u00a0bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. \u00a0If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Job Title Assistant Men's and Women's CC/Track & Field Coach - Part-Time Position Number 006852-00 Department Athletics: Joliet Job Grade Anticipated Salary Range $1,000-$3,000 Benefits Not benefit-eligible Notice of Nondiscrimination The University of St. Francis does not discriminate in its employment practices or in its educational programs on the basis of any protected class. The University also prohibits retaliation against any person opposing discrimination or harassment or participating in any internal or external investigation or complaint process related to allegations of misconduct. For a complete copy of USF\u2019s Policy on Equal Opportunity, Harassment, and Nondiscrimination for All Faculty, Students, Employees and Third Parties or for more information, please go to https://www.stfrancis.edu/titleix/ or contact the Title IX Coordinator at TitleIX@stfrancis.edu. Position Summary Assist the head men\u2019s and women\u2019s cross country/track & field coaches in coaching and leadership aspects of a model cross country and track & field program as they relate to academic commitment, supervision of staff and personnel, practice organization and instruction, meet preparation and recruitment. Essential Duties & Responsibilities Demonstrate respect for the Catholic and Franciscan values of the university. Demonstrate the ability to relate effectively to student-athletes, coaches, staff, administration and the University community. Participate in and promote a culture of continuing quality improvement. Assumption of coaching responsibilities related to the sports of men\u2019s and women\u2019s cross country and track & field. Provision of assistance in certain administrative responsibilities related to the sports of men\u2019s and women\u2019s cross country and track & field; in monitoring the academic progress of student-athletes; in the enforcement of team rules; in the planning, development and conducting of all in-season and off-season practices and conditioning sessions; in the instruction of staff. Ensure that proper safety guidelines and standards are maintained. Coordinate certain strategy related to the sports of men\u2019s and women\u2019s cross country and track & field. Responsible for certain aspects of recruitment in accordance with university and NAIA rules. Understanding and support of all athletic policies and regulations, as well as all philosophies, of the University, Chicagoland Collegiate Athletic Conference and National Association of Intercollegiate Athletics. Understanding and support of the NAIA Champions of Character Coaches Code. Represent the athletic department and university in a professional manner at various internal and external functions and in working with internal and external constituencies, including but not limited to the media and general public. Perform other administrative duties within the department as assigned. Must be able to work nights, weekends and holidays. Minimum Requirements High school diploma or GED . Three years as a cross country or track & field athlete or coaching experience. Ability to perform the physical requirements of the position. Ability and willingness to work nights, weekends and holidays. Willingness to support the Catholic and Franciscan values of the University. Preferred Requirements Bachelor\u2019s degree. Three years of collegiate cross country or track & field coaching experience. Hours/Shift/Work Schedule Hours vary, but do include weekends, nights and holidays. Physical Requirements of Position Work is performed in both an office setting and at athletic arenas with moderate exposure to varying weather conditions, but minimal health or safety hazards. Substantial time is spent working on a computer. This is sedentary work, which requires the following physical activities: sitting, walking, bending, stooping, finger dexterity, repetitive motions, talking, hearing and visual acuity. Travel is required. Hours of work include some nights, weekends and may include working up to 12 hours a day. Posting Detail Information Posting Number FP0785-16 Open Date 06/23/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other * Are you willing to uphold the Catholic and Franciscan values of the University? Yes No * Will you now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status (e.g., H-1B visa status)? Yes No * Please indicate your highest level of education: Less than GED/high school diploma GED/high school diploma Bachelor's degree Master's degree In a doctoral program ABD Doctorate * Are you available and willing to work weekends, nights and holidays? Yes No * Do you have experience as a Cross-Country/Track athlete or coach? Yes No * Please indicate your highest level of coaching experience in CC/Track & Field: Less than 3 years 3 - 5 years 5+ years I have at least 3 years of collegiate CC/Track & Field coaching experience Applicant Documents Required Documents Transcripts (unofficial are acceptable at time of application) Mission Response at https://pa-hrsuite-production.s3.amazonaws.com/856/docs/67939.pdf Resume Optional Documents The Annual Security & Fire Safety Report is published in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act. Clery - 2021 University of St. Francis Annual Security and Fire Safety Report A paper copy of this report is available by contacting the Safety & Security office at 815-740-3200. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://stfrancis.peopleadmin.com/postings/5790": {"title": "Security Officer - Part-time Weekends", "description": "University of St. Francis Employment Opportunities | Security Officer - Part-time Weekends Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help USF Website About Us Saints Stats Mission & History USF is Nationally Ranked Leadership Take a Virtual Tour USF Alumni & Family Relations Notice of Nondiscrimination Security Officer - Part-time Weekends Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to\u00a0bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. \u00a0If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Job Title Security Officer - Part-time Weekends Position Number 006239-00 Department Safety & Security - Joliet, IL Job Grade 5 Anticipated Salary Range $15.02-$16.52/hr Benefits Not benefit eligible Notice of Nondiscrimination The University of St. Francis does not discriminate in its employment practices or in its educational programs on the basis of any protected class. The University also prohibits retaliation against any person opposing discrimination or harassment or participating in any internal or external investigation or complaint process related to allegations of misconduct. For a complete copy of USF\u2019s Policy on Equal Opportunity, Harassment, and Nondiscrimination for All Faculty, Students, Employees and Third Parties or for more information, please go to https://www.stfrancis.edu/titleix/ or contact the Title IX Coordinator at TitleIX@stfrancis.edu. Position Summary To provide safety and security services for the protection of life and property to the university community. Essential Duties & Responsibilities Patrol assigned areas (university buildings, dormitories, parking lots) on foot or in a vehicle to ensure security, and to make presence known in a manner that contributes to the deterrence of security breaches Provide escort services for visitors, students, staff, faculty, and individuals responsible for transportation of moneys to or from university Prepare written and computerized reports of daily activity and incidents occurring in, on or around campus property Provide visible patrol and observe and report irregularities, such as fire hazards, leaking water pipes, missing signs, deficient parking lot surface conditions, and security doors left unlocked; sound alarm in case of fire or presence of unauthorized persons Perform periodic checks of emergency call boxes and/or streetlights to ensure proper functioning; report malfunctions Provide visible patrol and examine doors, windows, and gates to determine if they are secure Drive university vehicles, providing for the safe and efficient transportation to the university community and visitors Provide public assistance when requested, including lockout services and informationPerform other duties or assignments as required \u2022Participate in and promote a culture of continuing quality improvement Minimum Requirements 21 years of age High school diploma or GED Possess a valid Illinois driver\u2019s license Provision of a clear background check Ability to perform physical requirements of the position Ability to read, analyze and interpret instructions Ability to understand and adhere to all Safety and Security rules, regulations, policy and procedures, written memorandums, and verbal instructions issued by the director or his designee Ability to communicate effectively both orally and in writing Ability to apply firm and courteous instructions with the students, employees and visitors Ability to analyze situations quickly and objectively take the appropriate course of action Ability to establish and maintain cordial and effective working relationships with the university community Ability to gather data, compile information and prepare reports. Availability to work a varied work schedule encompassing all shifts Willingness to support the Catholic and Franciscan values of the university Preferred Requirements Hours/Shift/Work Schedule Saturday and Sunday Physical Requirements of Position This position requires to ability to walk, sit or stand for extended periods of time, run when necessary, climb stairs, lift up to 50 lbs. with no assistance, and to work in adverse weather conditions. The noise level in the work environment may sometimes be loud. Some work may be performed on a computer in an office setting with minimal exposure to health or safety hazards. Also requires the ability to perform the following physical activities: bending, stooping, reaching, finger dexterity, repetitive motions, talking, hearing and visual acuity. Posting Detail Information Posting Number FP0766-16 Open Date 03/23/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled No Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other * Are you willing to uphold the Catholic and Franciscan values of the University? Yes No * Please indicate your highest level of completed education: Less than GED/high school diploma GED/high school diploma Bachelor's degree Master's degree ABD Doctorate * How many years of experience do you have in this type of position? 0-1 1-3 3-5 5-7 7+ * Will you now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status (e.g., H-1B visa status)? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Transcripts (unofficial are acceptable at time of application) Cover Letter Mission Response at https://pa-hrsuite-production.s3.amazonaws.com/856/docs/67939.pdf Optional Documents The Annual Security & Fire Safety Report is published in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act. Clery - 2021 University of St. Francis Annual Security and Fire Safety Report A paper copy of this report is available by contacting the Safety & Security office at 815-740-3200. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://stfrancis.peopleadmin.com/postings/5789": {"title": "Undergrad Clinical Compliance Coordinator/Nursing Instructor/Asst Prof (Peds/OB)", "description": "University of St. Francis Employment Opportunities | Undergrad Clinical Compliance Coordinator/Nursing Instructor/Asst Prof (Peds/OB) Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help USF Website About Us Saints Stats Mission & History USF is Nationally Ranked Leadership Take a Virtual Tour USF Alumni & Family Relations Notice of Nondiscrimination Undergrad Clinical Compliance Coordinator/Nursing Instructor/Asst Prof (Peds/OB) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to\u00a0bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. \u00a0If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Review of applications begins immediately, and applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Unofficial transcripts are acceptable at the time of application. Salary and other considerations will be competitive and consistent with the university\u2019s commitment to recruiting the best-qualified individual. Submissions without all of the required materials may not be considered. Position Details Position Information Job Title Undergrad Clinical Compliance Coordinator/Nursing Instructor/Asst Prof (Peds/OB) Position Number 003359 Department Leach College of Nursing - Joliet, IL main campus Job Grade Anticipated Salary Range $62,000 annually for instructor-level; $72,000 annually for tenure-track Benefits stfrancis.edu/employment Notice of Nondiscrimination The University of St. Francis does not discriminate in its employment practices or in its educational programs on the basis of any protected class. The University also prohibits retaliation against any person opposing discrimination or harassment or participating in any internal or external investigation or complaint process related to allegations of misconduct. For a complete copy of USF\u2019s Policy on Equal Opportunity, Harassment, and Nondiscrimination for All Faculty, Students, Employees and Third Parties or for more information, please go to https://www.stfrancis.edu/titleix/ or contact the Title IX Coordinator at TitleIX@stfrancis.edu. Position Summary The University of St. Francis, a Catholic, Franciscan institution in Joliet, Illinois, invites applications for a nine-month, full-time faculty position as Undergrad Clinical Compliance Coordinator/Nursing Instructor/Asst Prof (Peds/OB) in the Leach College of Nursing, beginning August 2026. Rank will depend on the candidate\u2019s qualifications. We will consider candidates who hold a doctorate in Nursing or a related field. Interested applicants with limited teaching or leadership experience will be considered and enrolled in the Faculty Mentoring program, designed to develop them into seasoned faculty. This aligns with the Franciscan approach to developing academics, beginning where they are and using transformative approaches to academic development. The position reports to the Dean of Nursing, provides oversight of the undergrad clinical compliance, is expected to collaborate on curriculum, assessment, and other academic matters, and teaches courses. Our faculty is known for its commitment to education and nursing development through a leading-edge, student-focused educational methodology. The Leach College of Nursing offers CCNE -accredited undergraduate and graduate programs. We serve diverse students through a variety of learning modalities. Founded in 1920, The University of St. Francis is an award-winning, high-quality, Catholic, Franciscan university. The university is in a residential neighborhood 35 miles southwest of Chicago in downtown Joliet, IL. The surrounding Chicagoland area offers robust park and recreation resources, major league sports, cultural arts, museums, festivals, shopping, restaurants, and two major airports. The University of St. Francis is a welcoming community of learners committed to enhancing diversity and equity. Essential Duties & Responsibilities Uphold and fulfill the mission and philosophy of the Leach College of Nursing. Participate in and promote a culture of continuous quality improvement. The Undergraduate Clinical Compliance Coordinator is responsible for coordinating and monitoring student clinical compliance requirements for all enrolled undergraduate nursing students. This position supports regulatory, accreditation, agency, and clinical partner requirements to ensure that students are eligible to participate in clinical learning experiences. The coordinator serves as a liaison among students, faculty, clinical agencies, and university departments to maintain accurate compliance records and support successful clinical placement processes. Teach selected courses and participate in scholarly activities. Provide service to the University, Leach College of Nursing, and the community: Serve on appropriate University/College and Governance Committees; Participate in University/College activities including faculty, students, and alumni; Cooperate in the recruitment and retention of students; Engage in scholarly endeavors and research for professional and scholarly growth. Participate in professional programs and attend workshops and/or classes for personal enrichment; Participate in College projects in the area of expertise. Minimum Requirements Master\u2019s degree in nursing Current RN license or eligibility for licensing in Illinois Two years of experience in clinical nursing practice Teaching experience in baccalaureate nursing programs Evidence of self-development through participation in continuing education offerings, advanced study, scholarly pursuit, and/or professional and clinical activities Willingness to uphold and fulfill the mission, vision, values, and traditions of the University of St. Francis Ability to perform the physical requirements of the position Preferred Requirements DNP or Ph.D in nursing or related field Hours/Shift/Work Schedule This is a full-time, nine-month contract position, operating August through May each academic year. We offer a competitive compensation and benefits package. Work hours may vary based on program and clinical needs, and teaching responsibilities may include online courses. Course assignments may include day, evening, night, weekend, and summer offerings as needed. Physical Requirements of Position Work is performed in classroom and office settings with minimal exposure to health or safety hazards. Substantial time is spent working on a computer. This is sedentary work which requires the following physical activities: sitting, walking, bending, stooping, finger dexterity, repetitive motions, talking, hearing, and visual acuity. Posting Detail Information Posting Number FP0779-16 Open Date 05/22/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other * Are you willing to uphold the Catholic and Franciscan values of the University? Yes No * Will you now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status (e.g., H-1B visa status)? Yes No * Do you have a Master's of Science degree in Nursing? Yes No * Please indicate your highest level of education: Less than GED/high school diploma GED/high school diploma Bachelor's degree Master's degree In a doctoral program ABD Doctorate * Do you have a current Illinois RN license? Yes No * How many years of nursing work experience do you have? Less than 2 years 2 - 5 years More than 5 years * How many years of experience do you have as a nurse educator in classroom and clinical settings? Less than 2 2 - 4 5 - 7 8+ Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Transcripts (unofficial are acceptable at time of application) Statement of Teaching Philosophy License/Certification Mission Response at https://pa-hrsuite-production.s3.amazonaws.com/856/docs/67939.pdf Reference List - names and contact information of 3 additional references Optional Documents Plan for pursuit of doctorate in Nursing or related field The Annual Security & Fire Safety Report is published in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act. Clery - 2021 University of St. Francis Annual Security and Fire Safety Report A paper copy of this report is available by contacting the Safety & Security office at 815-740-3200. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://stfrancis.peopleadmin.com/postings/5762": {"title": "English Department Adjunct Faculty Fall 2026", "description": "University of St. Francis Employment Opportunities | English Department Adjunct Faculty Fall 2026 Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help USF Website About Us Saints Stats Mission & History USF is Nationally Ranked Leadership Take a Virtual Tour USF Alumni & Family Relations Notice of Nondiscrimination English Department Adjunct Faculty Fall 2026 Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to\u00a0bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. \u00a0If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This is a part-time adjunct teaching position located in Joliet, Illinois. The University of St. Francis is an equal opportunity employer. Position Details Position Information Job Title English Department Adjunct Faculty Fall 2026 Position Number XXXXXX-XX Department English & Foreign Languages - Adjunct Faculty Job Grade Anticipated Salary Range $905-$930 per credit hour Benefits Not benefits eligible Notice of Nondiscrimination The University of St. Francis does not discriminate in its employment practices or in its educational programs on the basis of any protected class. The University also prohibits retaliation against any person opposing discrimination or harassment or participating in any internal or external investigation or complaint process related to allegations of misconduct. For a complete copy of USF\u2019s Policy on Equal Opportunity, Harassment, and Nondiscrimination for All Faculty, Students, Employees and Third Parties or for more information, please go to https://www.stfrancis.edu/titleix/ or contact the Title IX Coordinator at TitleIX@stfrancis.edu. Position Summary The Department of English at the University of St. Francis invites applications for part-time adjunct faculty teaching opportunities for the 2026-27 academic year. The University of St. Francis is a welcoming community of learners committed to enhancing diversity and equity. Essential Duties & Responsibilities The University of St. Francis seeks qualified adjunct instructors to teach College Writing I, the first course in our two\u2011semester first\u2011year writing sequence, in person on our Joliet campus. Curriculum: Instructors design and teach College Writing I in alignment with our shared course description, outcomes, and the Illinois Articulation Initiative (C1900). The course introduces students to the writing process, rhetorical analysis, information literacy, academic argument, and citation. Responsibilities: Responsibilities include providing timely and substantive feedback on writing, maintaining an accurate gradebook in Canvas, and answering students\u2019 questions. Effective instructors support students through all stages of the writing process and design engaging in\u2011class activities that foster drafting, peer review, revision, and reflection. Additional Teaching Opportunities: Opportunities to teach Introduction to Literature may also be available. These courses introduce students to fiction, poetry, drama, and literary nonfiction, and most sections are in person. Minimum Requirements MA in English Willingness to uphold and fulfill the mission, vision, values, and traditions of the University of St. Francis Preferred Requirements Prior experience teaching first-year writing Available to teach on-campus in Joliet, IL Hours/Shift/Work Schedule Adjunct instructors may have the opportunity to teach up to six credit-hours per semester, or two courses. The work schedule is based on department needs and semester course schedules. Physical Requirements of Position Work performed in classroom settings with minimal exposure to health or safety hazards. This sedentary work which requires the following physical activities: sitting, walking, bending, stooping, finger dexterity, repetitive motions, talking, hearing and visual acuity. Posting Detail Information Posting Number FP0768-16 Open Date 04/14/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other * Are you willing to uphold the Catholic and Franciscan values of the University? Yes No * Will you now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status (e.g., H-1B visa status)? Yes No Please indicate your highest level of education: Less than GED/high school diploma GED/high school diploma Bachelor's degree Master's degree In a doctoral program ABD Doctorate Do you have teaching experience in higher education? Yes No How many years of relevant experience do you have? Less than 1 year 1 - 2 years 3 - 4 years 5 - 7 years More than 7 years Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Transcripts (unofficial are acceptable at time of application) Mission Response at https://pa-hrsuite-production.s3.amazonaws.com/856/docs/67939.pdf Optional Documents The Annual Security & Fire Safety Report is published in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act. Clery - 2021 University of St. Francis Annual Security and Fire Safety Report A paper copy of this report is available by contacting the Safety & Security office at 815-740-3200. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://stfrancis.peopleadmin.com/postings/5716": {"title": "Head Cheer Coach (Part-Time)", "description": "University of St. Francis Employment Opportunities | Head Cheer Coach (Part-Time) Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help USF Website About Us Saints Stats Mission & History USF is Nationally Ranked Leadership Take a Virtual Tour USF Alumni & Family Relations Notice of Nondiscrimination Head Cheer Coach (Part-Time) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to\u00a0bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. \u00a0If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Job Title Head Cheer Coach (Part-Time) Position Number NA Department Athletics: Joliet Job Grade N/A Anticipated Salary Range $10,000 Benefits None Notice of Nondiscrimination The University of St. Francis does not discriminate in its employment practices or in its educational programs on the basis of any protected class. The University also prohibits retaliation against any person opposing discrimination or harassment or participating in any internal or external investigation or complaint process related to allegations of misconduct. For a complete copy of USF\u2019s Policy on Equal Opportunity, Harassment, and Nondiscrimination for All Faculty, Students, Employees and Third Parties or for more information, please go to https://www.stfrancis.edu/titleix/ or contact the Title IX Coordinator at TitleIX@stfrancis.edu. Position Summary To oversee all coaching and leadership aspects of a model sideline and/or competitive cheer program as they relate to academic commitment, supervision of personnel, practice organization and instruction, match preparation, recruitment, scheduling and budget management. Essential Duties & Responsibilities Demonstrate respect for the Catholic and Franciscan values of the university. Demonstrate the ability to relate effectively to student-athletes, coaches, staff, administration and the University community. Participate in and promote a culture of continuing quality improvement. Assumption of all coaching responsibilities related to the sport of cheer. Assumption of all administrative responsibilities related to the sport of cheer, including purchase and maintenance of all equipment and coordination of food, lodging and transportation needs. Monitor the academic progress of student-athletes. Development and enforcement of team rules. Planning, development and conducting of all in-season and off-season practices and conditioning sessions. Ensure that proper safety guidelines and standards are maintained. Coordinate all strategy related to the sport of cheer. Responsible for all aspects of recruitment in accordance with university and NAIA rules, including meeting recruiting goals. A roster of 15 student-athletes is expected to be maintained. Ability to use social media for recruiting and program promoting purposes. Work in conjunction with athletic administration and Financial Aid Services in awarding financial assistance, specifically athletic scholarships. Understanding and support of all athletic policies and regulations, as well as all philosophies, of the University and National Association of Intercollegiate Athletics. Understanding and support of the NAIA Champions of Character Coaches Code. Work in conjunction with athletic administration in scheduling competitions and practices. Represent the athletic department and university in a professional manner at various internal and external functions and in working with internal and external constituencies, including but not limited to the media and general public. Oversee all aspects of budget preparation and management. Perform other administrative duties within the department as assigned. Must be able to work nights, weekends and holidays. Minimum Requirements High school diploma or GED . One year of cheer coaching experience. Ability to perform the physical requirements of the position. Ability and willingness to work nights, weekends and holidays. Willingness to support the Catholic and Franciscan values of the University. Preferred Requirements Bachelor\u2019s degree Three years of collegiate cheer coaching experience. Hours/Shift/Work Schedule Hours vary, but do include weekends, nights and holidays. Physical Requirements of Position Work is performed in both an office setting and at athletic arenas with moderate exposure to varying weather conditions, but minimal health or safety hazards. Substantial time is spent working on a computer. This is sedentary work, which requires the following physical activities: sitting, walking, bending, stooping, finger dexterity, repetitive motions, talking, hearing and visual acuity. Travel is required. Hours of work include some nights, weekends and may include working up to 12 hours a day. Posting Detail Information Posting Number FP0762-16 Open Date 02/15/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you willing to uphold the Catholic and Franciscan values of the University? Yes No * Do you have, or exceed, the minimum amount of relevant work experience as listing in our posting? Yes No * Will you now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status (e.g., H-1B visa status)? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Mission Response at https://pa-hrsuite-production.s3.amazonaws.com/856/docs/67939.pdf Optional Documents Transcripts (unofficial are acceptable at time of application) Letter of Recommendation 1 (you must upload something; letter writers may  send directly to Working@stfrancis.edu) Letter of Recommendation 2 (you must upload something; letter writers may  send directly to Working@stfrancis.edu) The Annual Security & Fire Safety Report is published in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act. Clery - 2021 University of St. Francis Annual Security and Fire Safety Report A paper copy of this report is available by contacting the Safety & Security office at 815-740-3200. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://stfrancis.peopleadmin.com/postings/5530": {"title": "Adjunct Faculty, Face-to-Face/Blended Classes, College of Business and Health Administration", "description": "University of St. Francis Employment Opportunities | Adjunct Faculty, Face-to-Face/Blended Classes, College of Business and Health Administration Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help USF Website About Us Saints Stats Mission & History USF is Nationally Ranked Leadership Take a Virtual Tour USF Alumni & Family Relations Notice of Nondiscrimination Adjunct Faculty, Face-to-Face/Blended Classes, College of Business and Health Administration Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to\u00a0bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. \u00a0If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Job Title Adjunct Faculty, Face-to-Face/Blended Classes, College of Business and Health Administration Position Number XXXXXX-00 Department School of Business - Joliet IL Job Grade Anticipated Salary Range $905-$981 (per credit hour) Benefits Not Benefits-Eligible Notice of Nondiscrimination The University of St. Francis does not discriminate in its employment practices or in its educational programs on the basis of any protected class. The University also prohibits retaliation against any person opposing discrimination or harassment or participating in any internal or external investigation or complaint process related to allegations of misconduct. For a complete copy of USF\u2019s Policy on Equal Opportunity, Harassment, and Nondiscrimination for All Faculty, Students, Employees and Third Parties or for more information, please go to https://www.stfrancis.edu/titleix/ or contact the Title IX Coordinator at TitleIX@stfrancis.edu. Position Summary The College of Business and Health Administration is a team of exceptional, experienced professionals dedicated to providing a rigorous academic curriculum in a supportive compassionate learning environment. Guided by our Catholic Franciscan values, we are committed to student success and lifelong learning. Faculty include both full-time and adjunct faculty who are professionals with expertise in the courses they teach. In addition, we are committed to continuous quality improvement, applied scholarly contribution, and assisting the business and health care communities. In a world driven by consumer choice, what sets the University of St. Francis apart from other higher learning institutions is the quality of our instructors. The University of St. Francis seeks educators who exhibit such a passion for teaching and learning that our College of Business and Health Administration ( COBHA ) students will have no doubt they are interacting with a quality instructor; one who is characterized by such adjectives as professional, prepared, prompt, patient, and positive. Today we are specifically looking for instructors willing to teach in person undergraduate courses in a variety of disciplines including accounting, finance, marketing, and management at our Joliet, IL location. Essential Duties & Responsibilities \u2022 Uphold and fulfill the mission and philosophy of the College of Business and Health Administration ( COBHA ) \u2022 Participate in and promote a culture of continuing quality improvement \u2022 Teach in person and blended courses on-site on our Joliet, IL campus \u2022 Participate in ongoing professional development activities and USF adjunct faculty training \u2022 Teach all assigned courses and hours as determined by the course schedule \u2022 Plan course instruction based upon approved curriculum, syllabus and learning outcomes \u2022 Design, administer and grade course assignments, essays and exams to assess student achievement as well as overall achievement of course learning outcomes Minimum Requirements \u2022 Master\u2019s degree in field \u2022 Evidence of strength in instructional methodology, delivery, and techniques \u2022 A willingness to support the Catholic and Franciscan values of the University \u2022 Ability to perform the physical requirements of the position \u2022 Ability and willingness to deliver on-site courses at our Joliet, IL campus according to the required schedule \u2022 Demonstrated experience working with individuals, ideally students, from other cultures and different backgrounds Preferred Requirements \u2022 Ph.D./ DBA /JD or other terminal doctoral degree in a variety of areas including management, marketing, business administration, finance, supply chain/logistics, international business, etc. \u2022 Two (2) years\u2019 teaching experience \u2022 Previous face-to-face teaching experience \u2022 Experience with Canvas Learning Management System Hours/Shift/Work Schedule Class schedules vary but generally fall to a Monday/Wednesday/Friday, Tuesday/Thursday or one evening/week schedule. There may be an option to teach a \u201cblended\u201d format. Physical Requirements of Position Work is performed in an office setting with minimal exposure to health or safety hazards. Substantial time is spent working on a computer. This is sedentary work which requires the following physical activities: sitting, walking, bending, stooping, finger dexterity, repetitive motions, talking, hearing and visual acuity. Posting Detail Information Posting Number FP0564-16 Open Date 05/23/2022 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * In what specific content area(s) would you like to instruct? (Open Ended Question) * How would you describe your technology proficiency? (Open Ended Question) * What do you believe separates you as an instructor from your peers? (Open Ended Question) * Do you have knowledge of Canvas learning management system? Yes No * What days and times are you available to teach face-to-face classes on our Joliet, IL campus? (Open Ended Question) * Are you willing to uphold the Catholic and Franciscan values of the University? Yes No * Will you now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status (e.g., H-1B visa status)? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Transcripts (unofficial are acceptable at time of application) Mission Response at https://pa-hrsuite-production.s3.amazonaws.com/856/docs/67939.pdf Optional Documents Letter of Recommendation 1 (you must upload something; letter writers may  send directly to Working@stfrancis.edu) Letter of Recommendation 2 (you must upload something; letter writers may  send directly to Working@stfrancis.edu) Statement of Teaching Philosophy Resume The Annual Security & Fire Safety Report is published in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act. Clery - 2021 University of St. Francis Annual Security and Fire Safety Report A paper copy of this report is available by contacting the Safety & Security office at 815-740-3200. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://stfrancis.peopleadmin.com/postings/5509": {"title": "Adjunct Faculty, International Programs, College of Business and Health Administration", "description": "University of St. Francis Employment Opportunities | Adjunct Faculty, International Programs, College of Business and Health Administration Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help USF Website About Us Saints Stats Mission & History USF is Nationally Ranked Leadership Take a Virtual Tour USF Alumni & Family Relations Notice of Nondiscrimination Adjunct Faculty, International Programs, College of Business and Health Administration Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to\u00a0bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. \u00a0If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Job Title Adjunct Faculty, International Programs, College of Business and Health Administration Position Number XXXXXX-00 Department COB Adjunct Faculty Job Grade Anticipated Salary Range $905-$981 (per credit hour) Benefits Not Benefit-Eligible Notice of Nondiscrimination The University of St. Francis does not discriminate in its employment practices or in its educational programs on the basis of any protected class. The University also prohibits retaliation against any person opposing discrimination or harassment or participating in any internal or external investigation or complaint process related to allegations of misconduct. For a complete copy of USF\u2019s Policy on Equal Opportunity, Harassment, and Nondiscrimination for All Faculty, Students, Employees and Third Parties or for more information, please go to https://www.stfrancis.edu/titleix/ or contact the Title IX Coordinator at TitleIX@stfrancis.edu. Position Summary The College of Business and Health Administration is a team of exceptional, experienced professionals dedicated to providing a rigorous academic curriculum in a supportive compassionate learning environment. Guided by our Catholic Franciscan values, we are committed to student success and lifelong learning. Faculty include both full-time and adjunct faculty who are professionals with expertise in the courses they teach. In addition, we are committed to continuous quality improvement, applied scholarly contribution, and assisting the business and health care communities. In a world driven by consumer choice, what sets the University of St. Francis apart from other higher learning institutions is the quality of our instructors. The University of St. Francis seeks educators who exhibit such a passion for teaching and learning that our College of Business and Health Administration ( COBHA ) students will have no doubt they are interacting with a quality instructor; one who is characterized by such adjectives as professional, prepared, prompt, patient, and positive. Today we are specifically looking for instructors excited to teach in person on location in our various international programs (currently in the Czech Republic and Vietnam) in a variety of bachelors and masters courses including management, finance, economics, marketing, supply chain, among others. Essential Duties & Responsibilities \u2022 Uphold and fulfill the mission and philosophy of the College of Business and Health Administration ( COBHA ) \u2022 Participate in and promote a culture of continuing quality improvement \u2022 Teach in person and blended courses on-site in our international locations \u2022 Participate in ongoing professional development activities and USF adjunct faculty training \u2022 Teach all assigned courses and hours as determined by the course schedule \u2022 Plan course instruction based upon approved curriculum, syllabus and learning outcomes \u2022 Design, administer and grade course assignments, essays and exams to assess student achievement as well as overall achievement of course learning outcomes \u2022 Follow the outlined travel and expense policies and procedures \u2022 Attend and/or participate in additional events while on location Minimum Requirements \u2022 Master\u2019s degree in field or equivalent professional experience \u2022 Evidence of strength in instructional methodology, delivery, and techniques \u2022 A willingness to support the Catholic and Franciscan values of the University \u2022 Ability to perform the physical requirements of the position \u2022 Ability and willingness to travel to international locations and deliver on-site courses according to the required schedule \u2022 Demonstrated experience working with individuals, ideally students, from other cultures and different backgrounds Preferred Requirements \u2022 Ph.D./ DBA /JD or other terminal doctoral degree in a variety of areas including management, marketing, business administration, finance, supply chain/logistics, international business, etc. \u2022 Five (5) years\u2019 teaching experience \u2022 Previous face-to-face teaching experience \u2022 Previous online teaching experience \u2022 Previous experience with traveling and teaching in international locations \u2022 Experience with Canvas Learning Management System Hours/Shift/Work Schedule Class schedules varies based upon the program but are generally about two weeks in duration Physical Requirements of Position Work is performed in an office setting with minimal exposure to health or safety hazards. Substantial time is spent working on a computer. This is sedentary work which requires the following physical activities: sitting, walking, bending, stooping, finger dexterity, repetitive motions, talking, hearing and visual acuity. Posting Detail Information Posting Number FP0725-16 Open Date 02/06/2025 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * In what specific content area(s) would you like to instruct? (Open Ended Question) * How would you describe your technology proficiency? (Open Ended Question) * What do you believe separates you as an instructor from your peers? (Open Ended Question) * What learning management systems (LMSs) have you used before to teach online? (Open Ended Question) * Tell us about your experience with international travel and/or teaching. (Open Ended Question) * Are you willing to uphold the Catholic and Franciscan values of the University? Yes No * I confirm that I am applying for an in-person/blended adjunct position that will require me to travel to an international location and deliver the content in person, and I am willing to do so if hired. Yes No * Will you now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status (e.g., H-1B visa status)? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Transcripts (unofficial are acceptable at time of application) Mission Response at https://pa-hrsuite-production.s3.amazonaws.com/856/docs/67939.pdf Optional Documents Letter of Recommendation 1 (you must upload something; letter writers may  send directly to Working@stfrancis.edu) Letter of Recommendation 2 (you must upload something; letter writers may  send directly to Working@stfrancis.edu) Statement of Teaching Philosophy The Annual Security & Fire Safety Report is published in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act. Clery - 2021 University of St. Francis Annual Security and Fire Safety Report A paper copy of this report is available by contacting the Safety & Security office at 815-740-3200. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://stfrancis.peopleadmin.com/postings/5431": {"title": "Adjunct instructor: Clinical Nursing, various specialties", "description": "University of St. Francis Employment Opportunities | Adjunct instructor: Clinical Nursing, various specialties Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help USF Website About Us Saints Stats Mission & History USF is Nationally Ranked Leadership Take a Virtual Tour USF Alumni & Family Relations Notice of Nondiscrimination Adjunct instructor: Clinical Nursing, various specialties Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. \u00a0To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to\u00a0bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. \u00a0If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Job Title Adjunct instructor: Clinical Nursing, various specialties Position Number SP3320-00 Department Leach College of Nursing - Joliet, IL main campus Job Grade Anticipated Salary Range $905- $981 (per credit hour) Benefits Not Benefit-Eligible Notice of Nondiscrimination The University of St. Francis does not discriminate in its employment practices or in its educational programs on the basis of any protected class. The University also prohibits retaliation against any person opposing discrimination or harassment or participating in any internal or external investigation or complaint process related to allegations of misconduct. For a complete copy of USF\u2019s Policy on Equal Opportunity, Harassment, and Nondiscrimination for All Faculty, Students, Employees and Third Parties or for more information, please go to https://www.stfrancis.edu/titleix/ or contact the Title IX Coordinator at TitleIX@stfrancis.edu. Position Summary Adjunct (part-time) faculty needed to teach in the following nursing clinical areas: medical-surgical pediatrics obstetrics psychiatric mental-health critical care The University of St. Francis is a welcoming community of learners committed to enhancing diversity and equity. Essential Duties & Responsibilities Teach nursing clinical courses in your specialty area to BSN students. Generally 12 hour clinicals once per week at various local and regional hospitals. Minimum Requirements Master\u2019s Degree in Nursing Current RN license Willingness to support the Catholic and Franciscan values of the university Preferred Requirements Two years\u2019 nursing work experience Teaching experience in higher education Hours/Shift/Work Schedule Based on availability. Depending on the site and unit, clinical may be on a Monday through Sunday during day or evening hours. Physical Requirements of Position Work is performed at clinical sites with some exposure to health or safety hazards. Requires sitting, walking, bending, stooping, finger dexterity, repetitive motions, talking, hearing, and visual acuity. Posting Detail Information Posting Number FP0550-16 Open Date 02/09/2022 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other * Are you willing to uphold the Catholic and Franciscan values of the University? Yes No * Will you now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status (e.g., H-1B visa status)? Yes No * Do you have a Master's of Science degree in Nursing? Yes No * How many years of nursing work experience do you have? Less than 2 years 2 - 5 years More than 5 years * Please indicate your teaching experience in higher education: Less than 1 year 1-3 years 4 + years Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Transcripts (unofficial are acceptable at time of application) Mission Response at https://pa-hrsuite-production.s3.amazonaws.com/856/docs/67939.pdf License/Certification Resume Letter of Recommendation 1 (you must upload something; letter writers may  send directly to Working@stfrancis.edu) Letter of Recommendation 2 (you must upload something; letter writers may  send directly to Working@stfrancis.edu) Letter of Recommendation 3 (you must upload something; letter writers may  send directly to Working@stfrancis.edu) Optional Documents The Annual Security & Fire Safety Report is published in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act. Clery - 2021 University of St. Francis Annual Security and Fire Safety Report A paper copy of this report is available by contacting the Safety & Security office at 815-740-3200. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://stfrancis.peopleadmin.com/postings/5909": {"title": "Communications Coordinator", "description": "University of St. Francis Employment Opportunities | Communications Coordinator Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help USF Website About Us Saints Stats Mission & History USF is Nationally Ranked Leadership Take a Virtual Tour USF Alumni & Family Relations Notice of Nondiscrimination Communications Coordinator Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Job Title Communications Coordinator Position Number 005909-00 Department Enrollment Support Services - Joliet IL Job Grade 7 Anticipated Salary Range $39,229-$43,128 Benefits https://stfrancis.edu/employment/ Notice of Nondiscrimination The University of St. Francis does not discriminate in its employment practices or in its educational programs on the basis of any protected class. The University also prohibits retaliation against any person opposing discrimination or harassment or participating in any internal or external investigation or complaint process related to allegations of misconduct. For a complete copy of USF\u2019s Policy on Equal Opportunity, Harassment, and Nondiscrimination for All Faculty, Students, Employees and Third Parties or for more information, please go to https://www.stfrancis.edu/titleix/ or contact the Title IX Coordinator at TitleIX@stfrancis.edu. Position Summary The Communications Coordinator is an hourly, non-exempt position that provides independent leadership and operational execution for enrollment communications supporting all student populations across the university. This position reports to the Admissions Operations Manager and is responsible for developing, coordinating, deploying, and assessing multichannel communication strategies that support recruitment, application completion, and enrollment conversion. This role oversees communication planning, campaign execution, content management, and workflow optimization within the university\u2019s customer relationship management ( CRM ) system environment while ensuring all messaging aligns with institutional priorities, branding standards, and audience needs. Essential Duties & Responsibilities Provide leadership for enrollment communications, ensuring alignment with divisional priorities and accountability for measurable outcomes related to recruitment and retention. Build, schedule, and deploy email and SMS campaigns designed to support movement of students through key stages of the enrollment lifecycle supporting all enrollment populations. Assess communication effectiveness and recommend improvements based on campaign performance data, enrollment trends, and identified operational needs. Maintain the comprehensive enrollment communication calendar and ensure timely execution of all scheduled communication initiatives. Collaborate with admissions staff and campus stakeholders to align communication priorities with enrollment goals and student engagement strategies. Maintain and update communication content blocks, templates, audience-specific messaging, and communication asset libraries within the CRM . Partner closely with Marketing Services to ensure enrollment communications align with institutional branding, messaging standards, and marketing priorities. Support the development of event-related communication content, landing pages, and promotional messaging. Build forms, portals, event pages, content snippets, and additional CRM components as directed. Maintain communication workflows and operational processes within the CRM to support efficient movement through enrollment pipelines. Provide regular reporting and recommendations to admissions and enrollment leadership regarding communication effectiveness and strategic opportunities. Oversee all outgoing letters, postcards, and brochures to prospective students. May assist with the supervision, training, and coordination of student workers supporting communication and content-related projects. Assist with data entry for new student applications as needed. Minimum Requirements Experience in higher education, marketing, communications or a related fieldExperience with Microsoft Word and ExcelExperience using a CRM or campus information system ( CIS ) Excellent written/interpersonal communication and organizational skills Detail-oriented, functions independently, self-starter Ability to work accurately in a fast-paced environment Strong prioritization skills Willingness to support the Catholic and Franciscan values of the university Preferred Requirements Experience with SCT Banner (or other educational enterprise resource system) and Element451 (or other customer relationship management system) Proficiency with Microsoft Word and Excel Bachelor\u2019s degree Hours/Shift/Work Schedule Work is typically conducted Monday-Friday, between 8 a.m. \u2013 5 p.m., but may also require some evenings and weekends as necessary. Physical Requirements of Position Work is performed in an office setting with minimal exposure to health or safety hazards. Substantial time is spent working on a computer. This is sedentary work which requires the following physical activities: sitting, walking, bending, stooping, finger dexterity, repetitive motions, talking, hearing and visual acuity. Posting Detail Information Posting Number FP0788-16 Open Date 10/14/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you meet or exceed the minimum qualifications as listed in this posting? Yes No * Please briefly explain the software, applications or tools you have used\u2014and the extent to which you feel comfortable using them\u2014to produce short- or long-form videos for promotional use. (Open Ended Question) * Will you now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status (e.g., H-1B visa status)? Yes No * How would you describe your writing skills? Basic Intermediate Advanced Superior * Are you willing to uphold the Catholic and Franciscan values of the University? Yes No * Do you have experience using a Customer Relationship Management (CRM) system? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Transcripts (unofficial are acceptable at time of application) Mission Response at https://pa-hrsuite-production.s3.amazonaws.com/856/docs/67939.pdf Work/Writing Sample Optional Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Recommendation 1 (you must upload something; letter writers may send directly to Working@stfrancis.edu) Letter of Recommendation 2 (you must upload something; letter writers may send directly to Working@stfrancis.edu) Letter of Recommendation 3 (you must upload something; letter writers may send directly to Working@stfrancis.edu) The Annual Security & Fire Safety Report is published in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act. Clery - 2021 University of St. Francis Annual Security and Fire Safety Report A paper copy of this report is available by contacting the Safety & Security office at 815-740-3200. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}}, "rows": {"https://stfrancis.peopleadmin.com/postings/5907": {"school_id": 395, "posting_url": "https://stfrancis.peopleadmin.com/postings/5907", "job_title_in_post": "Retention Specialist", "position_type": "Non-academic", "job_term": "Part-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://stfrancis.peopleadmin.com/postings/5906": {"school_id": 395, "posting_url": "https://stfrancis.peopleadmin.com/postings/5906", "job_title_in_post": "Residence Life Coordinator", "position_type": "Non-academic", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://stfrancis.peopleadmin.com/postings/5905": {"school_id": 395, "posting_url": "https://stfrancis.peopleadmin.com/postings/5905", "job_title_in_post": "Security Officer - full time", "position_type": "Non-academic", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://stfrancis.peopleadmin.com/postings/5902": {"school_id": 395, "posting_url": "https://stfrancis.peopleadmin.com/postings/5902", "job_title_in_post": "Graduate Assistant for Student Life", "position_type": "Non-academic", "job_term": "Full-time", "de